{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.linker.closure\n     2\t  \"The module closure walker (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md section\n     3\t   4.2): a pure function over a `dao.jing` handle that answers whether\n     4\t   every blob a module manifest needs -- the manifest, every row of its\n     5\t   tree, its three derivation records, the three lowered images, and the\n     6\t   closure of every required manifest -- is held locally and passes its\n     7\t   shape and address checks.  It reads bytes through the handle with a\n     8\t   sentinel, performs no stream operation, and never throws for absent or\n     9\t   invalid content: the first absent blob ends the walk `:missing`, the\n    10\t   first failed check `:invalid`.\n    11\t\n    12\t   It verifies shape and address only.  It does not re-lower, discharge\n    13\t   or judge names: `yin.vm.linker/link-manifest` does, afterwards, against\n    14\t   the same store.\"\n    15\t  (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:typed_data\" :as typed]])\n    16\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    17\t            [yin.vm.linker :as linker]))\n    18\t\n    19\t\n    20\t(def lowered-formats\n    21\t  \"The derivation formats a manifest names, in walk order, each with its\n    22\t   format record (for the image's identity check).\"\n    23\t  [[:yin.semantic/code linker/semantic-format]\n    24\t   [:yin.debruijn.code linker/stack-format]\n    25\t   [:yin.debruijn.register linker/register-format]])\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\t(defn- byte-count\n    29\t  [bs]\n    30\t  #?(:cljd (.-length ^typed/Uint8List bs)\n    31\t     :clj (alength ^bytes bs)\n    32\t     :cljs (.-length bs)))\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t(defn- stop\n    36\t  \"`st` ended by the terminal `outcome`.\"\n    37\t  [st outcome]\n    38\t  (assoc st :stop outcome))\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\t(defn- missing\n    42\t  [address role path]\n    43\t  {:yin.link.closure/outcome :missing\n    44\t   :address address :role role :path path})\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\t(defn- invalid\n    48\t  ([address role path code] (invalid address role path code nil))\n    49\t  ([address role path code detail]\n    50\t   {:yin.link.closure/outcome :invalid\n    51\t    :address address :role role :path path\n    52\t    :defect (cond-> {:code code} (some? detail) (assoc :detail detail))}))\n    53\t\n    54\t\n    55\t(defn- read-blob\n    56\t  \"Read `address` as the walk's next blob: `[st value]`, or `[st' nil]`\n    57\t   with `st'` stopped.  A blob read before is answered from the walk's\n    58\t   own memory and counted once.  Order: absent, address, then the parts\n    59\t   and bytes bounds, then decoding.\"\n    60\t  [st address role path]\n    61\t  (if (contains? (:seen st) address)\n    62\t    [st (get (:seen st) address)]\n    63\t    (let [{:keys [handle sentinel bounds parts bytes]} st\n    64\t          bs (if (jing/segment-address? address)\n    65\t               ((:get-bytes-fn handle) address sentinel)\n    66\t               sentinel)]\n    67\t      (cond\n    68\t        (not (jing/segment-address? address))\n    69\t        [(stop st (invalid address role path :address-mismatch)) nil]\n    70\t\n    71\t        (identical? sentinel bs)\n    72\t        [(stop st (missing address role path)) nil]\n    73\t\n    74\t        (not (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bs))\n    75\t        [(stop st (invalid address role path :address-mismatch)) nil]\n    76\t\n    77\t        (>= parts (:max-parts bounds))\n    78\t        [(stop st (invalid address role path :parts-limit {:bound :max-parts}))\n    79\t         nil]\n    80\t\n    81\t        (> (+ bytes (byte-count bs)) (:max-bytes bounds))\n    82\t        [(stop st (invalid address role path :parts-limit {:bound :max-bytes}))\n    83\t         nil]\n    84\t\n    85\t        :else\n    86\t        (let [value (try (jing/segment-value address bs)\n    87\t                         (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n    88\t                           sentinel))]\n    89\t          (if (identical? sentinel value)\n    90\t            [(stop st (invalid address role path :address-mismatch)) nil]\n    91\t            [(-> st\n    92\t                 (update :parts inc)\n    93\t                 (update :bytes + (byte-count bs))\n    94\t                 (assoc-in [:seen address] value))\n    95\t             value]))))))\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\t(defn- walk-rows\n    99\t  \"Step 2: a bounded worklist over the grammar's child slots from the\n   100\t   tree root, each row checked row-locally before its children are\n   101\t   followed.\"\n   102\t  [st tree path]\n   103\t  (loop [st st\n   104\t         queue [[tree 0]]\n   105\t         enqueued #{tree}]\n   106\t    (if (empty? queue)\n   107\t      st\n   108\t      (let [[address depth] (first queue)]\n   109\t        (if (> depth (get-in st [:bounds :max-depth]))\n   110\t          (stop st (invalid address :row path :parts-limit {:bound :max-depth}))\n   111\t          (let [[st body] (read-blob st address :row path)]\n   112\t            (cond\n   113\t              (:stop st) st\n   114\t\n   115\t              (linker/row-local-defect body)\n   116\t              (stop st (invalid address :row path :row-defect\n   117\t                                (linker/row-local-defect body)))\n   118\t\n   119\t              :else\n   120\t              (let [kids (remove enqueued\n   121\t                                 (distinct ((:parts-fn linker/ast-format) body)))]\n   122\t                (recur st\n   123\t                       (into (subvec queue 1)\n   124\t                             (map (fn [k] [k (inc depth)]))\n   125\t                             kids)\n   126\t                       (into enqueued kids))))))))))\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\t(defn- walk-records\n   130\t  \"Step 3: each derivation record the manifest names, checked as a\n   131\t   record leading from the manifest's tree.  Answers `st` with the\n   132\t   records under `:records`, keyed by format.\"\n   133\t  [st manifest path]\n   134\t  (reduce (fn [st [format-kw _]]\n   135\t            (if-some [address (get (:yin.module/derivations manifest) format-kw)]\n   136\t              (let [[st record] (read-blob st address :record path)]\n   137\t                (cond\n   138\t                  (:stop st) (reduced st)\n   139\t\n   140\t                  (linker/record-defect record)\n   141\t                  (reduced (stop st (invalid address :record path :record-defect\n   142\t                                             (linker/record-defect record))))\n   143\t\n   144\t                  (not= (:yin.module/tree manifest) (:yin.ledger/input record))\n   145\t                  (reduced (stop st (invalid address :record path\n   146\t                                             :derivation-mismatch\n   147\t                                             {:expected (:yin.module/tree manifest)\n   148\t                                              :actual (:yin.ledger/input record)})))\n   149\t\n   150\t                  :else (assoc-in st [:records format-kw] record)))\n   151\t              st))\n   152\t          (assoc st :records {})\n   153\t          lowered-formats))\n   154\t\n   155\t\n   156\t(defn- walk-images\n   157\t  \"Step 4: the image each record's output identifies, at the identity\n   158\t   itself for the semantic vector and at the manifest's index entry for H\n   159\t   and R, held to its format's identity check.\"\n   160\t  [st manifest path]\n   161\t  (reduce (fn [st [format-kw record-format]]\n   162\t            (if-some [record (get (:records st) format-kw)]\n   163\t              (let [identity (:yin.ledger/output record)\n   164\t                    address (if (= :yin.semantic/code format-kw)\n   165\t                              identity\n   166\t                              (get (:yin.module/index manifest) identity))]\n   167\t                (if (nil? address)\n   168\t                  (reduced (stop st (invalid nil :image path :index-entry-missing\n   169\t                                             {:format format-kw\n   170\t                                              :identity identity})))\n   171\t                  (let [[st image] (read-blob st address :image path)]\n   172\t                    (cond\n   173\t                      (:stop st) (reduced st)\n   174\t\n   175\t                      (not (try ((:identity-matches-fn record-format) identity image)\n   176\t                                (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   177\t                                  false)))\n   178\t                      (reduced (stop st (invalid address :image path\n   179\t                                                 :identity-mismatch\n   180\t                                                 {:format format-kw\n   181\t                                                  :identity identity})))\n   182\t\n   183\t                      :else st))))\n   184\t              st))\n   185\t          st\n   186\t          lowered-formats))\n   187\t\n   188\t\n   189\t(declare walk-module)\n   190\t\n   191\t\n   192\t(defn- walk-requires\n   193\t  \"Step 5: list every requirement of the module, then walk each required\n   194\t   manifest not walked before, one level deeper.\"\n   195\t  [st manifest-address manifest path depth]\n   196\t  (reduce (fn [st [n pinned]]\n   197\t            (let [st (update st :requires conj\n   198\t                             {:module manifest-address :name n :manifest pinned})]\n   199\t              (cond\n   200\t                (contains? (:visited st) pinned) st\n   201\t\n   202\t                (> (inc depth) (get-in st [:bounds :max-depth]))\n   203\t                (reduced (stop st (invalid pinned :require (conj path pinned)\n   204\t                                           :parts-limit {:bound :max-depth})))\n   205\t\n   206\t                :else\n   207\t                (let [st (walk-module st pinned :require path (inc depth))]\n   208\t                  (if (:stop st) (reduced st) st)))))\n   209\t          st\n   210\t          (sort-by (fn [[n _]] (str n)) (:yin.module/requires manifest))))\n   211\t\n   212\t\n   213\t(defn- walk-module\n   214\t  [st manifest-address role path depth]\n   215\t  (let [path (conj path manifest-address)\n   216\t        [st manifest] (read-blob st manifest-address role path)]\n   217\t    (cond\n   218\t      (:stop st) st\n   219\t\n   220\t      (linker/manifest-defect manifest)\n   221\t      (stop st (invalid manifest-address role path :manifest-defect\n   222\t                        (linker/manifest-defect manifest)))\n   223\t\n   224\t      :else\n   225\t      (let [st (-> st\n   226\t                   (update :visited conj manifest-address)\n   227\t                   (update :modules conj manifest-address)\n   228\t                   (walk-rows (:yin.module/tree manifest) path))\n   229\t            st (if (:stop st) st (walk-records st manifest path))\n   230\t            st (if (:stop st) st (walk-images st manifest path))]\n   231\t        (if (:stop st)\n   232\t          st\n   233\t          (walk-requires st manifest-address manifest path depth))))))\n   234\t\n   235\t\n   236\t(defn walk\n   237\t  \"Walk the closure of `manifest-address` in `handle` (section 4.2), with\n   238\t   `opts` `{:bounds {:max-parts n :max-depth d :max-bytes b}}`, every\n   239\t   bound left out taking `yin.vm.linker/default-bounds`.  Answers exactly\n   240\t   one of:\n   241\t\n   242\t     {:yin.link.closure/outcome :missing\n   243\t      :address a :role role :path [...]}\n   244\t     {:yin.link.closure/outcome :complete\n   245\t      :manifest m :blobs n :modules [m ...]\n   246\t      :requires [{:module m :name n :manifest pinned} ...]}\n   247\t     {:yin.link.closure/outcome :invalid\n   248\t      :address a :role role :path [...] :defect {:code c :detail d}}\n   249\t\n   250\t   `role` is `:manifest`, `:row`, `:record`, `:image` or `:require`;\n   251\t   `path` the manifest addresses from the root to the module the blob\n   252\t   belongs to.  `:code` is one of `:address-mismatch`, `:manifest-defect`,\n   253\t   `:row-defect`, `:record-defect`, `:derivation-mismatch`,\n   254\t   `:index-entry-missing`, `:identity-mismatch`, `:parts-limit`.\"\n   255\t  ([handle manifest-address] (walk handle manifest-address nil))\n   256\t  ([handle manifest-address opts]\n   257\t   (let [bounds (into linker/default-bounds\n   258\t                      (keep (fn [[k v]] (when (some? v) [k v])))\n   259\t                      (:bounds opts))\n   260\t         st (walk-module {:handle handle\n   261\t                          :sentinel #?(:cljd (Object.) :clj (Object.) :cljs (js-obj))\n   262\t                          :bounds bounds\n   263\t                          :parts 0\n   264\t                          :bytes 0\n   265\t                          :seen {}\n   266\t                          :visited #{}\n   267\t                          :modules []\n   268\t                          :requires []}\n   269\t                         manifest-address :manifest [] 0)]\n   270\t     (or (:stop st)\n   271\t         {:yin.link.closure/outcome :complete\n   272\t          :manifest manifest-address\n   273\t          :blobs (count (:seen st))\n   274\t          :modules (:modules st)\n   275\t          :requires (:requires st)}))))\n     1\t(ns yin.vm.linker.dht\n     2\t  \"The linker over `dao.jing.dht`, as plain Clojure (docs/design/\n     3\t   yin.vm.linker.dht.md sections 4, 5.4, 7 and 10; slice L2): publish a\n     4\t   module through a `dao.space.dht` node, load its closure onto another\n     5\t   node by manifest address, check its dependency names against the\n     6\t   reader's own name environment, and link it over the node's local store.\n     7\t\n     8\t   The load is `dao.space.dht/load` with the closure walker of\n     9\t   `yin.vm.linker.closure` as its walk: the node stays the only step\n    10\t   owner and fetches each blob the walk answers missing.  A link runs\n    11\t   only after the whole closure is `:loaded`, over a local runtime on the\n    12\t   node's own store, so it asks no peer for anything.\n    13\t\n    14\t   Names come from the reader's composition: the principals it declares\n    15\t   and the index snapshots it chose to load.  Nothing here is read from an\n    16\t   index as authority, and nothing depends on `yin.repl`.\"\n    17\t  (:require [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    18\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n    19\t            [dao.space.dht :as dht]\n    20\t            [dao.space.index :as index]\n    21\t            [dao.space.store :as durable]\n    22\t            [dao.space.store.fs :as fs]\n    23\t            [yin.vm.linker :as linker]\n    24\t            [yin.vm.linker.authority :as authority]\n    25\t            [yin.vm.linker.closure :as closure]\n    26\t            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n    27\t            [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]))\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\t(def module-kind\n    31\t  \"The `:kind` of a module closure load.\"\n    32\t  :yin.module/manifest)\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t(defn- refused\n    36\t  [reason data]\n    37\t  (merge {:status :refused :reason reason} data))\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t;; =============================================================================\n    41\t;; Publication (5.4)\n    42\t;; =============================================================================\n    43\t\n    44\t(defn publish!\n    45\t  \"`publish-module!` on the node's store: the blobs join the node's\n    46\t   current publication window, reported by the announcement that closes\n    47\t   it.\"\n    48\t  [node spec]\n    49\t  (publish/publish-module! (dht/store node) spec))\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(defn publish-name!\n    53\t  \"Publish the module `name` exporting `exports`, derived from the\n    54\t   publisher's own index `db` (`module-from-index`, section 5.3), through\n    55\t   the node's store, and sign what binds the name to it (6.6): answers\n    56\t   `{:status :ok :address a :links {...} :envelopes [...]}`, each envelope\n    57\t   `publish/assertion`'s answer, for the caller to enter into its index\n    58\t   as one transaction (6.1) before it announces.  Without `key` it is\n    59\t   refused `:yin.link.publish/no-key`; any refusal writes nothing.\n    60\t   `opts` also carries `module-from-index`'s `:primitives`, `:modules`\n    61\t   and `:host-modules`.\"\n    62\t  [node db {:keys [key name] :as opts}]\n    63\t  (if-not key\n    64\t    (refused :yin.link.publish/no-key {:name name})\n    65\t    (let [spec (publish/module-from-index db opts)\n    66\t          res (if (= :refused (:status spec)) spec (publish! node spec))]\n    67\t      (if (= :refused (:status res))\n    68\t        res\n    69\t        (assoc (select-keys res [:address :links])\n    70\t               :status :ok\n    71\t               :envelopes (publish/name-envelopes db key name (:address res)))))))\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t;; =============================================================================\n    75\t;; The module load (4.3)\n    76\t;; =============================================================================\n    77\t\n    78\t(defn closure-walk\n    79\t  \"The closure walk of `manifest-address` as a `dao.space.dht` load walk:\n    80\t   the walker's three outcomes in the load's three shapes.\"\n    81\t  [manifest-address]\n    82\t  (fn [handle]\n    83\t    (let [w (closure/walk handle manifest-address)]\n    84\t      (case (:yin.link.closure/outcome w)\n    85\t        :missing {::dht/walk :missing :address (:address w)}\n    86\t        :complete {::dht/walk :complete :value w}\n    87\t        :invalid {::dht/walk :invalid :address (:address w) :defect (:defect w)}))))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn load-module\n    91\t  \"Start loading the closure of `manifest-address` onto `node`; answers\n    92\t   the node.  `dao.space.dht/step` fetches what is missing.\"\n    93\t  [node manifest-address]\n    94\t  (dht/load node manifest-address {:kind module-kind\n    95\t                                   :walk (closure-walk manifest-address)}))\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\t(defn module-status\n    99\t  \"The load status of `manifest-address` (4.3), or nil.\"\n   100\t  [node manifest-address]\n   101\t  (dht/load-status node manifest-address))\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t(defn load-refusal\n   105\t  \"The section 9 response row of a failed closure load: `status` as\n   106\t   `module-status` answers it.  `:miss` is `:absent` with the miss\n   107\t   `:cause`, `:invalid` is `:descriptor-defect` with the defect's `:code`\n   108\t   (and its `:detail` and `:text` when present), and `:unaskable` is\n   109\t   `:yin.link.dht/unaskable` with the client's `:outcome`.  nil for a load\n   110\t   that has not failed.  The DHT link source refuses with it.\"\n   111\t  [status]\n   112\t  (when (= :failed (:status status))\n   113\t    (let [{::dht/keys [failure] :keys [address cause defect outcome]} (:reason status)]\n   114\t      (case failure\n   115\t        :miss (refused :absent {:address address :cause cause})\n   116\t        :invalid (refused :descriptor-defect\n   117\t                          (merge {:address address :code (:code defect)}\n   118\t                                 (select-keys defect [:detail :text])))\n   119\t        :unaskable (refused :yin.link.dht/unaskable\n   120\t                            {:address address :outcome outcome})))))\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t(defn- not-loaded\n   124\t  [node manifest-address]\n   125\t  (refused :yin.link.dht/not-loaded\n   126\t           {:address manifest-address\n   127\t            :load (dissoc (module-status node manifest-address) :value)}))\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(defn- loaded-closure\n   131\t  [node manifest-address]\n   132\t  (let [status (module-status node manifest-address)]\n   133\t    (when (and (= :loaded (:status status)) (= module-kind (:kind status)))\n   134\t      (:value status))))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t;; =============================================================================\n   138\t;; Names: the snapshot set and the fold (7.2, 7.3)\n   139\t;; =============================================================================\n   140\t\n   141\t(defn head\n   142\t  \"The manifest the HEAD of the node's directory names, or nil: a node\n   143\t   over a durable directory store (`dao.space.store`) has one once its\n   144\t   publisher has written it; any other node has none.\"\n   145\t  [node]\n   146\t  (when-some [dir (:durable-dir (dht/local node))]\n   147\t    (some-> (fs/read-file-text dir durable/head-name)\n   148\t            str/trim\n   149\t            edn/read-string\n   150\t            :manifest)))\n   151\t\n   152\t\n   153\t(defn snapshots\n   154\t  \"The node's snapshot set (7.2) as the sorted vector of its addresses:\n   155\t   the manifest its directory's HEAD names, when there is one, and every\n   156\t   index manifest whose load is `:loaded`.  Nothing else in the local\n   157\t   store is considered.\"\n   158\t  [node]\n   159\t  (vec (sort-by str (distinct (cond-> (vec (dht/loaded-indexes node))\n   160\t                                (head node) (conj (head node)))))))\n   161\t\n   162\t\n   163\t(defn- snapshot-datoms\n   164\t  \"The datoms of the snapshot `s`: a loaded index's, or HEAD's read from\n   165\t   the node's own store.\"\n   166\t  [node s]\n   167\t  (or (dht/loaded-datoms node s)\n   168\t      (index/read-datoms (dht/local node) s)))\n   169\t\n   170\t\n   171\t(defn- snapshot-events\n   172\t  \"The authority events of every snapshot, assembled per snapshot (an\n   173\t   entity id is local to its index) and concatenated in snapshot order,\n   174\t   each envelope with its proof once.\"\n   175\t  [node snapshot]\n   176\t  (into []\n   177\t        (comp (mapcat (fn [s]\n   178\t                        (authority/events-from-datoms\n   179\t                          (filter (fn [[_ a]]\n   180\t                                    (contains? #{:yin.module/envelope\n   181\t                                                 :yin.module/proof}\n   182\t                                               a))\n   183\t                                  (snapshot-datoms node s)))))\n   184\t              (distinct))\n   185\t        snapshot))\n   186\t\n   187\t\n   188\t(defn authority\n   189\t  \"The reader's authority from its composition (7.1): each declared\n   190\t   public key (64 lowercase hex) a principal whose proof is an Ed25519\n   191\t   signature (6.3), at `:seq-floor` 0, and `name-env`'s direct entries.\"\n   192\t  [{:keys [principals name-env]}]\n   193\t  {:principals (into {}\n   194\t                     (map (fn [public]\n   195\t                            [(sign/principal public)\n   196\t                             {:proof :yin.module/signature\n   197\t                              :key public\n   198\t                              :verify sign/verify-envelope\n   199\t                              :seq-floor 0}]))\n   200\t                     principals)\n   201\t   :name-env (or name-env {})})\n   202\t\n   203\t\n   204\t(defn- fold\n   205\t  \"The fold of the reader's snapshot set under `authority`\n   206\t   `{:principals {principal declaration} :name-env {name address}}`, and\n   207\t   every envelope it saw by id.  A retraction whose target is not an\n   208\t   assertion the snapshot set holds -- none, or another retraction --\n   209\t   names no name, so its diagnostic moves from `:diagnostics` to\n   210\t   `:global-diagnostics`, once (owner decision 6).\"\n   211\t  [node authority]\n   212\t  (let [snapshot (snapshots node)\n   213\t        events (snapshot-events node snapshot)\n   214\t        env (authority/name-environment\n   215\t              {:snapshot snapshot :principals (or (:principals authority) {})}\n   216\t              events)\n   217\t        envelopes (into {}\n   218\t                        (map (fn [e]\n   219\t                               (let [env (:yin.module/envelope e)]\n   220\t                                 [(authority/assertion-id env) env])))\n   221\t                        events)\n   222\t        ;; global unless the target is an assertion in the set: only an\n   223\t        ;; assertion carries a name\n   224\t        global? (fn [d]\n   225\t                  (and (= :dangling-retraction (:reason d))\n   226\t                       (not= :assert (:yin.module/op (get envelopes (:of d))))))]\n   227\t    {:env (-> env\n   228\t              (assoc :diagnostics (filterv (complement global?) (:diagnostics env))\n   229\t                     :global-diagnostics (filterv global? (:diagnostics env)))\n   230\t              (update :names into\n   231\t                      (map (fn [[n address]]\n   232\t                             [n {:status :ok :address address\n   233\t                                 :yin.link/provenance :composition}]))\n   234\t                      (:name-env authority)))\n   235\t     :envelopes envelopes}))\n   236\t\n   237\t\n   238\t(defn names\n   239\t  \"The reader's name environment: `authority/name-environment` over the\n   240\t   envelopes of the loaded index snapshots, under the principals\n   241\t   `authority` declares, with its direct `:name-env` entries winning,\n   242\t   their provenance `:composition`.  A retraction whose target is not an\n   243\t   assertion in the snapshot set (an assertion outside it, or a\n   244\t   retraction) is under `:global-diagnostics`, once, with\n   245\t   its `:principal` and the assertion id it names under `:of`; it is in\n   246\t   no per-name diagnostic.\"\n   247\t  [node authority]\n   248\t  (:env (fold node authority)))\n   249\t\n   250\t\n   251\t(defn- diagnostics-for\n   252\t  \"The fold's diagnostics whose envelope binds or retracts `n`.\"\n   253\t  [{:keys [env envelopes]} n]\n   254\t  (let [name-of (fn [e]\n   255\t                  (if (= :retract (:yin.module/op e))\n   256\t                    (:yin.module/name (get envelopes (:yin.module/of e)))\n   257\t                    (:yin.module/name e)))]\n   258\t    (filterv (fn [d] (= n (name-of (get envelopes (:id d)))))\n   259\t             (:diagnostics env))))\n   260\t\n   261\t\n   262\t(defn resolve-name\n   263\t  \"The name `n` in the reader's name environment: its `names` entry when\n   264\t   it resolves, else its section 9 refusal -- `:absent` with the fold's\n   265\t   `:diagnostics` for that name, or `:ambiguous-name` with every\n   266\t   `:addresses` and `:asserters`.\"\n   267\t  [node authority n]\n   268\t  (let [folded (fold node authority)\n   269\t        entry (get-in folded [:env :names n])]\n   270\t    (cond\n   271\t      (= :ok (:status entry)) entry\n   272\t\n   273\t      (= :ambiguous-name (:reason entry))\n   274\t      (refused :ambiguous-name (merge {:name n}\n   275\t                                      (select-keys entry [:addresses :asserters])))\n   276\t\n   277\t      :else\n   278\t      (refused :absent {:name n :diagnostics (diagnostics-for folded n)}))))\n   279\t\n   280\t\n   281\t;; =============================================================================\n   282\t;; Dependency bindings (7.4)\n   283\t;; =============================================================================\n   284\t\n   285\t\n   286\t(defn dependency-bindings\n   287\t  \"One entry per requirement of the loaded closure of `manifest-address`,\n   288\t   in walk order: whether the dependency's name resolves, in the reader's\n   289\t   own name environment, to the address its publisher pinned.  `:binding`\n   290\t   is `:ok`, `:absent` (with the fold's `:diagnostics` for that name),\n   291\t   `:ambiguous` (`:addresses`, `:asserters`) or `:mismatch` (`:resolved`,\n   292\t   `:asserters`).  Refused `:yin.link.dht/not-loaded` unless the closure\n   293\t   is `:loaded`.\"\n   294\t  [node authority manifest-address]\n   295\t  (if-some [w (loaded-closure node manifest-address)]\n   296\t    (let [folded (fold node authority)]\n   297\t      (mapv (fn [{:keys [module name manifest]}]\n   298\t              (let [entry (get-in folded [:env :names name])\n   299\t                    base {:module module :name name :pinned manifest}\n   300\t                    asserters (get-in entry [:yin.link/provenance\n   301\t                                             :yin.module/asserted-by])]\n   302\t                (cond\n   303\t                  (= :ambiguous-name (:reason entry))\n   304\t                  (assoc base :binding :ambiguous\n   305\t                         :addresses (:addresses entry)\n   306\t                         :asserters (:asserters entry))\n   307\t\n   308\t                  (not= :ok (:status entry))\n   309\t                  (assoc base :binding :absent\n   310\t                         :diagnostics (diagnostics-for folded name))\n   311\t\n   312\t                  (= manifest (:address entry))\n   313\t                  (assoc base :binding :ok)\n   314\t\n   315\t                  :else\n   316\t                  (assoc base :binding :mismatch\n   317\t                         :resolved (:address entry)\n   318\t                         :asserters (or asserters [:composition])))))\n   319\t            (:requires w)))\n   320\t    (not-loaded node manifest-address)))\n   321\t\n   322\t\n   323\t;; =============================================================================\n   324\t;; Link (4.1 step 4)\n   325\t;; =============================================================================\n   326\t\n   327\t(defn link\n   328\t  \"`link-manifest` of `format-kw` through `manifest-address` over the\n   329\t   node's local store, `:verifying` with discharge deferred unless `opts`\n   330\t   says otherwise.  Refused `:yin.link.dht/not-loaded` unless the closure\n   331\t   is `:loaded`; a link refused `:absent` after it is a walker defect,\n   332\t   `:yin.link.dht/closure-incomplete`.\"\n   333\t  ([node manifest-address format-kw]\n   334\t   (link node manifest-address format-kw nil))\n   335\t  ([node manifest-address format-kw opts]\n   336\t   (let [format (some #(when (= format-kw (:format %)) %) publish/code-formats)]\n   337\t     (cond\n   338\t       (nil? (loaded-closure node manifest-address))\n   339\t       (not-loaded node manifest-address)\n   340\t\n   341\t       (nil? format)\n   342\t       (linker/refused :unsupported-format {:format format-kw})\n   343\t\n   344\t       :else\n   345\t       (let [res (publish/link-local (dht/local node) manifest-address format opts)]\n   346\t         (if (= :absent (:reason res))\n   347\t           (refused :yin.link.dht/closure-incomplete {:address (:address res)})\n   348\t           res))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yin/vm/linker/closure_test.cljc | sed -n '273,335p'; rg -n 'malformed|empty-export|empty.exports' test/yin/vm/linker/{dht,publish}_test.cljc; nl -ba test/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yin/vm/linker/closure_test.cljc | sed -n '273,335p'; rg -n 'malformed|empty-export|empty.exports' test/yin/vm/linker/{dht,publish}_test.cljc; nl -ba test/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   273\t;; =============================================================================\n   274\t\n   275\t(deftest each-closed-code-is-produced\n   276\t  (let [fixtures (invalid-fixtures)]\n   277\t    (is (= #{:address-mismatch :manifest-defect :row-defect :record-defect\n   278\t             :derivation-mismatch :index-entry-missing :identity-mismatch\n   279\t             :parts-limit}\n   280\t           (set (map first fixtures))))\n   281\t    (doseq [[code store address opts] fixtures]\n   282\t      (testing (name code)\n   283\t        (let [w (closure/walk store address opts)]\n   284\t          (is (= :invalid (:yin.link.closure/outcome w)) (pr-str w))\n   285\t          (is (= code (get-in w [:defect :code])) (pr-str w)))))))\n   286\t\n   287\t\n   288\t(def malformed-values\n   289\t  \"Values no manifest key accepts, of every collection and scalar kind.\"\n   290\t  [42 [1] \"bad\" #{1} '(1) :k {1 2} [[1 2]]])\n   291\t\n   292\t\n   293\t(defn- defect-or-throw\n   294\t  [manifest]\n   295\t  (try (linker/manifest-defect manifest)\n   296\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   297\t         {::threw (str e)})))\n   298\t\n   299\t\n   300\t(deftest the-manifest-validator-is-total-over-every-key\n   301\t  (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n   302\t        manifest (:manifest (publish-base! store))]\n   303\t    (is (nil? (linker/manifest-defect manifest)) \"the published manifest is valid\")\n   304\t    (doseq [k (sort-by str (conj (set (keys manifest)) :yin.module/index))\n   305\t            v malformed-values]\n   306\t      (testing (str k \" \" (pr-str v))\n   307\t        (let [bad (assoc manifest k v)\n   308\t              d (defect-or-throw bad)\n   309\t              m (jing/materialize! store bad)\n   310\t              w (try (closure/walk store m)\n   311\t                     (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   312\t                       {::threw (str e)}))]\n   313\t          (is (map? d) (pr-str d))\n   314\t          (is (not (contains? d ::threw)) (pr-str d))\n   315\t          (is (= [:invalid m :manifest-defect]\n   316\t                 [(:yin.link.closure/outcome w) (:address w) (get-in w [:defect :code])])\n   317\t              (str \"the walk is total: \" (pr-str w))))))))\n   318\t\n   319\t\n   320\t(deftest a-malformed-optional-index-is-a-manifest-defect-naming-the-manifest\n   321\t  (doseq [bad [42 [1] \"bad\"]]\n   322\t    (testing (pr-str bad)\n   323\t      (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n   324\t            res (publish-base! store)\n   325\t            m (with-manifest store (assoc (:manifest res) :yin.module/index bad))]\n   326\t        (is (= {:rule :manifest-shape :key :yin.module/index}\n   327\t               (defect-or-throw (jing/get store m nil))))\n   328\t        (is (= {:yin.link.closure/outcome :invalid :address m :role :manifest :path [m]\n   329\t                :defect {:code :manifest-defect\n   330\t                         :detail {:rule :manifest-shape :key :yin.module/index}}}\n   331\t               (select-keys (closure/walk store m)\n   332\t                            [:yin.link.closure/outcome :address :role :path :defect])))))))\n   333\t\n   334\t\n   335\t(deftest each-bound-is-a-parts-limit\ntest/yin/vm/linker/dht_test.cljc:309:(deftest a-malformed-optional-index-fails-the-load-as-a-manifest-defect\ntest/yin/vm/linker/publish_test.cljc:53:(deftest malformed-definition-refuses-as-data\ntest/yin/vm/linker/publish_test.cljc:55:        malformed (app (assoc (var-node 'yin/def) :source :extra)\ntest/yin/vm/linker/publish_test.cljc:58:                 store {:name 'bad :ast malformed :exports #{}\ntest/yin/vm/linker/publish_test.cljc:61:    (is (= :yin.link.publish/malformed-tree (:reason result)))))\ntest/yin/vm/linker/publish_test.cljc:77:(deftest a-required-manifest-with-a-malformed-index-refuses-as-data\ntest/yin/vm/linker/publish_test.cljc:280:(deftest an-empty-export-list-is-the-canonical-no-op-module\n     1\t(ns yin.vm.linker.dht-end-to-end-test\n     2\t  \"Linker over DHT slice L5, in process (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md\n     3\t   section 12, L5): the end-to-end scenario of yin.repl.dht-process-test\n     4\t   over the dao.jing.dht test mesh seam, so that it runs on the JVM, Node\n     5\t   and Dart alike.\n     6\t\n     7\t   A publishing shell holding an Ed25519 key defines a function and a\n     8\t   module-level value, and publishes `my.lib` (the function) and\n     9\t   `my.store` (an export reading the value) by name.  A reader shell\n    10\t   handed the publisher's index manifest (`--dht-manifest`) and its\n    11\t   principal (`--dht-principal`) requires each module by name, waits\n    12\t   through pending, and evaluates the export, on each of the four VMs.\n    13\t   The name resolves only through a verified signature: a reader that\n    14\t   does not declare the principal, and one handed an index whose proof\n    15\t   another key made, are each refused `:absent` with the fold's\n    16\t   diagnostic.  Time advances only by the readings each step is handed.\"\n    17\t  (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:io\" :as dart-io]])\n    18\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n    19\t            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    20\t            [dao.datom :as datom]\n    21\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    22\t            [dao.jing.dht :as jing.dht]\n    23\t            [dao.jing.dht.mesh :as mesh]\n    24\t            [dao.space.dht :as dht]\n    25\t            [dao.space.dht-test :as dht-test]\n    26\t            [dao.space.index :as index]\n    27\t            [yin.repl :as repl]\n    28\t            [yin.repl.dht :as repl.dht]\n    29\t            [yin.repl.store :as store]\n    30\t            [yin.vm.linker.dht :as ld]\n    31\t            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n    32\t            [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]))\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t;; =============================================================================\n    36\t;; Host helpers\n    37\t;; =============================================================================\n    38\t\n    39\t(defn- temp-dir\n    40\t  []\n    41\t  (str \"target/test-linker-e2e-\" (random-uuid)))\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\t(defn- cleanup-dir!\n    45\t  [dir]\n    46\t  #?(:cljd (try (.deleteSync (dart-io/Directory. dir) .recursive true)\n    47\t                (catch Object _ nil))\n    48\t     :clj (let [f (java.io.File. ^String dir)]\n    49\t            (when (.isDirectory f)\n    50\t              (doseq [child (.listFiles f)]\n    51\t                (.delete ^java.io.File child))\n    52\t              (.delete f)))\n    53\t     :cljs (try (.rmSync (js/require \"fs\") dir #js {:recursive true :force true})\n    54\t                (catch :default _ nil))))\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\t;; =============================================================================\n    58\t;; A mesh world of shells and plain publishing peers\n    59\t;; =============================================================================\n    60\t\n    61\t(defn- peer-node\n    62\t  [net port]\n    63\t  (let [c (mesh/join! net port {::jing.dht/publish? true\n    64\t                                ::jing.dht/max-inbound-bytes (* 64 1024 1024)})]\n    65\t    {:composition c :state (jing.dht/state c)}))\n    66\t\n    67\t\n    68\t(defn- step-peers\n    69\t  [peers now]\n    70\t  (into {}\n    71\t        (map (fn [[port {:keys [composition state]}]]\n    72\t               (mesh/tick! composition now)\n    73\t               [port {:composition composition\n    74\t                      :state (jing.dht/step state 256)}]))\n    75\t        peers))\n    76\t\n    77\t\n    78\t(defn- shell-at\n    79\t  \"A shell over a dht store at `dir` on mesh `port` with contacts\n    80\t   `peer-ports`: publishing when `key` is given (`--dht-publish\n    81\t   --dht-key`), hydrating `manifest` first when given (`--dht-manifest`),\n    82\t   declaring `principals` (`--dht-principal`).\"\n    83\t  [net dir port peer-ports {:keys [key manifest principals]}]\n    84\t  (repl/create-state\n    85\t    {:index-store-spec {:type :dht\n    86\t                        :dir dir\n    87\t                        :peers (mapv (fn [p] {:host \"127.0.0.1\" :port p}) peer-ports)\n    88\t                        :publish? (some? key)\n    89\t                        :bind-host \"127.0.0.1\"\n    90\t                        :bind-port 0\n    91\t                        :bind! (mesh/seam net port)\n    92\t                        :max-inbound-bytes repl.dht/default-max-inbound-bytes\n    93\t                        :manifest manifest}\n    94\t     :dht-key key\n    95\t     :principals (vec principals)}))\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\t(defn- world\n    99\t  [net peer-ports]\n   100\t  {:net net\n   101\t   :peers (into {} (map (fn [p] [p (peer-node net p)])) peer-ports)\n   102\t   :shells {}\n   103\t   :now 0\n   104\t   :lines []\n   105\t   :events []})\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\t(defn- step-world\n   109\t  \"One reading: every shell's node (`yin.repl.dht/step`, then the\n   110\t   re-check its load events call for, as the host ticker does), then\n   111\t   every peer.\"\n   112\t  [w]\n   113\t  (let [now (:now w)\n   114\t        stepped (map (fn [[k s]]\n   115\t                       (let [[s lines events] (repl.dht/step s now)\n   116\t                             [s text] (repl/recheck-on-load-events s events)]\n   117\t                         [k s (cond-> lines text (conj text))\n   118\t                          (map #(assoc % :who k) events)]))\n   119\t                     (:shells w))]\n   120\t    (-> w\n   121\t        (assoc :shells (into {} (map (fn [[k s]] [k s])) stepped)\n   122\t               :peers (step-peers (:peers w) now)\n   123\t               :now (+ now 10))\n   124\t        (update :lines into (mapcat #(nth % 2)) stepped)\n   125\t        (update :events into (mapcat #(nth % 3)) stepped))))\n   126\t\n   127\t\n   128\t(defn- run-world\n   129\t  \"Step `w` until `(done? w)`; `{:failure cause}` under `:failure` when\n   130\t   `limit` readings pass first.\"\n   131\t  [w limit cause done?]\n   132\t  (loop [w w]\n   133\t    (cond\n   134\t      (done? w) w\n   135\t      (> (:now w) limit) (assoc w :failure (str cause \" within \" limit \" readings\"))\n   136\t      :else (recur (step-world w)))))\n   137\t\n   138\t\n   139\t(defn- eval-at\n   140\t  \"Evaluate `line` at shell `k`'s prompt: `[w text]`.\"\n   141\t  [w k line]\n   142\t  (let [[s text] (repl/eval-input (get-in w [:shells k]) line)]\n   143\t    [(assoc-in w [:shells k] s) text]))\n   144\t\n   145\t\n   146\t(defn- head-of\n   147\t  [w k]\n   148\t  (get-in w [:shells k :indexer :manifest-address]))\n   149\t\n   150\t\n   151\t(defn- published\n   152\t  [w k manifest]\n   153\t  (some #(when (and (= k (:who %)) (= :published (::dht/event %))\n   154\t                    (= manifest (:manifest %)))\n   155\t           %)\n   156\t        (:events w)))\n   157\t\n   158\t\n   159\t(defn- last-response\n   160\t  [w k]\n   161\t  (dissoc (peek (mesh/values (get-in w [:shells k :link-pair :responses])))\n   162\t          :yin.link/id))\n   163\t\n   164\t\n   165\t(defn- close-all!\n   166\t  [w]\n   167\t  (doseq [[_ s] (:shells w)] (store/close! (:index-store s)))\n   168\t  nil)\n   169\t\n   170\t\n   171\t;; =============================================================================\n   172\t;; The scenario\n   173\t;; =============================================================================\n   174\t\n   175\t(def ^:private publisher-lines\n   176\t  [\"(def f (fn [x] (+ x 4200)))\"\n   177\t   \"(def base 7)\"\n   178\t   \"(def g (fn [] (+ base 1)))\"\n   179\t   \"(require (quote yin.link))\"\n   180\t   \"(yin.link/publish (quote my.lib) (quote [f]))\"\n   181\t   \"(yin.link/publish (quote my.store) (quote [g]))\"])\n   182\t\n   183\t\n   184\t(defn- publish-world\n   185\t  \"Peers at 2 and 3 and the publisher `:a` at 1, which types\n   186\t   `publisher-lines` and settles: `[w manifest]`, its HEAD index manifest\n   187\t   reported acknowledged.\"\n   188\t  [net dir key]\n   189\t  (let [w (-> (world net [2 3])\n   190\t              (assoc-in [:shells :a] (shell-at net dir 1 [2 3] {:key key})))\n   191\t        w (reduce (fn [w line] (first (eval-at w :a line))) w publisher-lines)\n   192\t        m (head-of w :a)\n   193\t        w (run-world w 60000 \"the publisher's HEAD was not reported\"\n   194\t                     #(published % :a m))]\n   195\t    (is (nil? (:failure w)) (:failure w))\n   196\t    (is (= :acknowledged (:result (published w :a m)))\n   197\t        (pr-str (dissoc (published w :a m) :failed)))\n   198\t    [w m]))\n   199\t\n   200\t\n   201\t(defn- hydrate\n   202\t  \"Add reader `k` at mesh `port`, handed `manifest`, and run until it\n   203\t   admits evaluation.\"\n   204\t  [w k dir port manifest principals]\n   205\t  (let [w (assoc-in w [:shells k]\n   206\t                    (shell-at (:net w) dir port [2 3 1]\n   207\t                              {:manifest manifest :principals principals}))\n   208\t        w (run-world w (+ (:now w) 60000) (str (name k) \" did not hydrate\")\n   209\t                     #(repl.dht/admitting? (get-in % [:shells k])))]\n   210\t    (is (nil? (:failure w)) (:failure w))\n   211\t    (is (nil? (repl.dht/refusal (get-in w [:shells k]))))\n   212\t    w))\n   213\t\n   214\t\n   215\t(defn- require-at\n   216\t  \"Require `module` at shell `k` and run until the run ends: `[w text]`,\n   217\t   the require's own text.\"\n   218\t  [w k module]\n   219\t  (let [[w text] (eval-at w k (str \"(require (quote \" module \"))\"))\n   220\t        w (run-world w (+ (:now w) 120000) (str \"the require of \" module \" never ended\")\n   221\t                     #(nil? (get-in % [:shells k :pending-run])))]\n   222\t    (is (nil? (:failure w)) (:failure w))\n   223\t    [w text]))\n   224\t\n   225\t\n   226\t(def ^:private vm-types\n   227\t  [:ast-walker :semantic :stack :register])\n   228\t\n   229\t\n   230\t(deftest a-reader-requires-a-published-module-by-name-on-all-four-vms\n   231\t  (let [[adir bdir] [(temp-dir) (temp-dir)]\n   232\t        net (mesh/mesh)\n   233\t        key (sign/generate)\n   234\t        principal (sign/principal (:public key))]\n   235\t    (try\n   236\t      (let [[w m] (publish-world net adir key)\n   237\t            w (hydrate w :b bdir 4 m [(:public key)])\n   238\t            names (ld/names (get-in w [:shells :b :dht])\n   239\t                            (ld/authority {:principals [(:public key)]}))]\n   240\t        (testing \"the reader resolves both names, each signed by the publisher\"\n   241\t          (doseq [n '[my.lib my.store]]\n   242\t            (is (= [principal] (get-in names [:names n :yin.link/provenance\n   243\t                                              :yin.module/asserted-by]))\n   244\t                (pr-str (get-in names [:names n])))))\n   245\t        (reduce\n   246\t          (fn [w vm-type]\n   247\t            (let [[w _] (eval-at w :b (str \"(vm \" vm-type \")\"))\n   248\t                  [w text] (require-at w :b 'my.lib)\n   249\t                  linked (get-in w [:shells :b :last-value])\n   250\t                  lib-response (last-response w :b)\n   251\t                  [w answer] (eval-at w :b \"(my.lib/f 1)\")\n   252\t                  [w _] (require-at w :b 'my.store)\n   253\t                  store-response (last-response w :b)\n   254\t                  [_ value] (eval-at w :b \"(my.store/g)\")]\n   255\t              (testing (name vm-type)\n   256\t                (when (= :ast-walker vm-type)\n   257\t                  (is (str/includes? text \"pending\")\n   258\t                      \"the first require waits on the closure load\"))\n   259\t                (is (= 'my.lib linked) (pr-str lib-response))\n   260\t                (is (= \"4201\" answer))\n   261\t                (testing \"the store corpus\"\n   262\t                  (when (= :ast-walker vm-type)\n   263\t                    (is (= {:status :refused :reason :undeclared-free :name 'base}\n   264\t                           (select-keys store-response [:status :reason :name]))\n   265\t                        (str \"the linker's reason, naming the read: \"\n   266\t                             (pr-str store-response))))\n   267\t                  (when-not (= :ast-walker vm-type)\n   268\t                    (is (= :ok (:status store-response)) (pr-str store-response))\n   269\t                    (is (= \"8\" value))))\n   270\t                nil)\n   271\t              w))\n   272\t          w\n   273\t          vm-types)\n   274\t        (close-all! w))\n   275\t      (finally\n   276\t        (run! cleanup-dir! [adir bdir])))))\n   277\t\n   278\t\n   279\t(deftest without-the-principal-the-require-is-absent-undeclared\n   280\t  (let [[adir cdir] [(temp-dir) (temp-dir)]\n   281\t        net (mesh/mesh)\n   282\t        key (sign/generate)]\n   283\t    (try\n   284\t      (let [[w m] (publish-world net adir key)\n   285\t            w (hydrate w :c cdir 5 m [])\n   286\t            [w _] (require-at w :c 'my.lib)\n   287\t            body (last-response w :c)]\n   288\t        (is (= {:status :refused :reason :absent :name 'my.lib}\n   289\t               (select-keys body [:status :reason :name]))\n   290\t            (pr-str body))\n   291\t        (is (= [[:undeclared-principal (sign/principal (:public key))]]\n   292\t               (mapv (juxt :reason :principal) (:diagnostics body))))\n   293\t        (is (nil? (get-in w [:shells :c :last-value])))\n   294\t        (close-all! w))\n   295\t      (finally\n   296\t        (run! cleanup-dir! [adir cdir])))))\n   297\t\n   298\t\n   299\t(deftest a-dangling-retraction-is-one-global-diagnostic-at-the-prompt\n   300\t  (let [[adir edir] [(temp-dir) (temp-dir)]\n   301\t        net (mesh/mesh)\n   302\t        key (sign/generate)\n   303\t        principal (sign/principal (:public key))\n   304\t        ;; an assertion signed but never published: no snapshot holds it\n   305\t        unpublished (:envelope (publish/assertion key {:name 'my.lib\n   306\t                                                       :manifest (jing/segment-key \"elsewhere\")\n   307\t                                                       :seq 90}))\n   308\t        of (jing/segment-key unpublished)]\n   309\t    (try\n   310\t      (let [[w _] (publish-world net adir key)\n   311\t            node (get-in w [:shells :a :dht])\n   312\t            dangling (let [r (publish/retraction key {:of of :seq 91})]\n   313\t                       (dht-test/publish-datoms!\n   314\t                         node\n   315\t                         [{:db/id datom/first-user-id\n   316\t                           :yin.module/envelope (:envelope r)\n   317\t                           :yin.module/proof (:proof r)}]))\n   318\t            w (run-world w (+ (:now w) 60000) \"the retraction index was not reported\"\n   319\t                         #(published % :a dangling))\n   320\t            w (hydrate w :e edir 7 dangling [(:public key)])\n   321\t            [w _] (eval-at w :e \"(require (quote yin.link))\")\n   322\t            [w _] (eval-at w :e \"(yin.link/names)\")\n   323\t            env (get-in w [:shells :e :last-value])]\n   324\t        (is (nil? (:failure w)) (:failure w))\n   325\t        (testing \"(yin.link/names) carries it once, globally, with principal and id\"\n   326\t          (is (= [[:dangling-retraction principal of]]\n   327\t                 (mapv (juxt :reason :principal :of) (:global-diagnostics env)))\n   328\t              (pr-str env)))\n   329\t        (testing \"and in no per-name diagnostic\"\n   330\t          (is (not-any? #(= :dangling-retraction (:reason %)) (:diagnostics env))\n   331\t              (pr-str (:diagnostics env))))\n   332\t        (testing \"a require of the name it would have retracted is absent, no diagnostic\"\n   333\t          (let [[w _] (require-at w :e 'my.lib)]\n   334\t            (is (= {:status :refused :reason :absent :name 'my.lib :diagnostics []}\n   335\t                   (last-response w :e)))\n   336\t            (close-all! w))))\n   337\t      (finally\n   338\t        (run! cleanup-dir! [adir edir])))))\n   339\t\n   340\t\n   341\t(deftest a-retraction-of-a-retraction-is-global-at-the-prompt\n   342\t  (let [[adir edir] [(temp-dir) (temp-dir)]\n   343\t        net (mesh/mesh)\n   344\t        key (sign/generate)\n   345\t        principal (sign/principal (:public key))\n   346\t        unpublished (:envelope (publish/assertion key {:name 'my.lib\n   347\t                                                       :manifest (jing/segment-key \"elsewhere\")\n   348\t                                                       :seq 90}))\n   349\t        r1 (publish/retraction key {:of (jing/segment-key unpublished) :seq 91})\n   350\t        r1-id (jing/segment-key (:envelope r1))\n   351\t        ;; its target is a retraction, which carries no name\n   352\t        r2 (publish/retraction key {:of r1-id :seq 92})]\n   353\t    (try\n   354\t      (let [[w _] (publish-world net adir key)\n   355\t            index (dht-test/publish-datoms!\n   356\t                    (get-in w [:shells :a :dht])\n   357\t                    (vec (map-indexed (fn [i r]\n   358\t                                        {:db/id (+ datom/first-user-id i)\n   359\t                                         :yin.module/envelope (:envelope r)\n   360\t                                         :yin.module/proof (:proof r)})\n   361\t                                      [r1 r2])))\n   362\t            w (run-world w (+ (:now w) 60000) \"the retraction index was not reported\"\n   363\t                         #(published % :a index))\n   364\t            w (hydrate w :e edir 8 index [(:public key)])\n   365\t            [w _] (eval-at w :e \"(require (quote yin.link))\")\n   366\t            [w _] (eval-at w :e \"(yin.link/names)\")\n   367\t            env (get-in w [:shells :e :last-value])]\n   368\t        (is (nil? (:failure w)) (:failure w))\n   369\t        (testing \"(yin.link/names): both retractions are global, each once\"\n   370\t          (is (= #{[:dangling-retraction principal (jing/segment-key unpublished)]\n   371\t                   [:dangling-retraction principal r1-id]}\n   372\t                 (set (mapv (juxt :reason :principal :of) (:global-diagnostics env))))\n   373\t              (pr-str env))\n   374\t          (is (= 2 (count (:global-diagnostics env)))))\n   375\t        (testing \"and neither is a per-name diagnostic\"\n   376\t          (is (not-any? #(= :dangling-retraction (:reason %)) (:diagnostics env))\n   377\t              (pr-str (:diagnostics env))))\n   378\t        (close-all! w))\n   379\t      (finally\n   380\t        (run! cleanup-dir! [adir edir])))))\n   381\t\n   382\t\n   383\t(deftest an-empty-export-list-publishes-the-no-op-module-at-the-prompt\n   384\t  (let [[adir bdir] [(temp-dir) (temp-dir)]\n   385\t        net (mesh/mesh)\n   386\t        key (sign/generate)]\n   387\t    (try\n   388\t      (let [[w _] (publish-world net adir key)\n   389\t            [w text] (eval-at w :a \"(yin.link/publish (quote empty.lib) (quote []))\")\n   390\t            res (get-in w [:shells :a :last-value])\n   391\t            m (head-of w :a)\n   392\t            w (run-world w (+ (:now w) 60000) \"the publisher's HEAD was not reported\"\n   393\t                         #(published % :a m))]\n   394\t        (testing \"answered as data, not thrown\"\n   395\t          (is (= 'empty.lib (:module res)) text)\n   396\t          (is (= {:yin.ast/code :ok :yin.semantic/code :ok\n   397\t                  :yin.debruijn.code :ok :yin.debruijn.register :ok}\n   398\t                 (:links res))\n   399\t              text))\n   400\t        (testing \"a reader requires it by name on every VM\"\n   401\t          (let [w (hydrate w :b bdir 9 m [(:public key)])\n   402\t                w (reduce (fn [w vm-type]\n   403\t                            (let [[w _] (eval-at w :b (str \"(vm \" vm-type \")\"))\n   404\t                                  [w _] (require-at w :b 'empty.lib)]\n   405\t                              (is (= 'empty.lib (get-in w [:shells :b :last-value]))\n   406\t                                  (str vm-type \" \" (pr-str (last-response w :b))))\n   407\t                              w))\n   408\t                        w\n   409\t                        vm-types)]\n   410\t            (close-all! w))))\n   411\t      (finally\n   412\t        (run! cleanup-dir! [adir bdir])))))\n   413\t\n   414\t\n   415\t(defn- forged-index!\n   416\t  \"The publisher's HEAD index `m` with every proof replaced by one `key`\n   417\t   made over another envelope, published and announced through the\n   418\t   publisher's own node: its name claims, proofs that do not verify.\"\n   419\t  [node m key]\n   420\t  (dht-test/publish-datoms!\n   421\t    node\n   422\t    (into []\n   423\t          (comp (filter (fn [[_ a]] (= :yin.module/envelope a)))\n   424\t                (map-indexed (fn [i [_ _ env]]\n   425\t                               {:db/id (+ datom/first-user-id i)\n   426\t                                :yin.module/envelope env\n   427\t                                :yin.module/proof (sign/sign-envelope\n   428\t                                                    (:seed key)\n   429\t                                                    (update env :yin.module/seq + 1000))})))\n   430\t          (index/read-datoms (dht/local node) m))))\n   431\t\n   432\t\n   433\t(deftest a-proof-over-another-envelope-does-not-resolve\n   434\t  (let [[adir ddir] [(temp-dir) (temp-dir)]\n   435\t        net (mesh/mesh)\n   436\t        key (sign/generate)]\n   437\t    (try\n   438\t      (let [[w m] (publish-world net adir key)\n   439\t            forged (forged-index! (get-in w [:shells :a :dht]) m key)\n   440\t            w (run-world w (+ (:now w) 60000) \"the forged index was not reported\"\n   441\t                         #(published % :a forged))\n   442\t            w (hydrate w :d ddir 6 forged [(:public key)])\n   443\t            [w _] (require-at w :d 'my.lib)\n   444\t            body (last-response w :d)]\n   445\t        (is (nil? (:failure w)) (:failure w))\n   446\t        (is (= {:status :refused :reason :absent :name 'my.lib}\n   447\t               (select-keys body [:status :reason :name]))\n   448\t            (pr-str body))\n   449\t        (is (= [[:unauthenticated :bad-proof]]\n   450\t               (mapv (juxt :reason :kind) (:diagnostics body)))\n   451\t            \"the signature was verified, and failed\")\n   452\t        (close-all! w))\n   453\t      (finally\n   454\t        (run! cleanup-dir! [adir ddir])))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
