{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc | sed -n '1,250p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc | sed -n '123,204p;267,400p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc | sed -n '270,390p'; rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(deftest|plain-clojure-leg|keygen|reader-b|4201|load-refusal' test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/index.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc | sed -n '1,250p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc | sed -n '123,204p;267,400p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc | sed -n '270,390p'; rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(deftest|plain-clojure-leg|keygen|reader-b|4201|load-refusal' test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.repl.index\n     2\t  \"The shell's code indexer: a `dao.space.index` observer on `program-out`\n     3\t   (docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md).\n     4\t\n     5\t   It is a peer of the evaluator's observer on the same medium, attached\n     6\t   independently and advanced by the evaluation round, never by the\n     7\t   evaluator: neither knows the other.  Each expanded tree packet `[root\n     8\t   rows]` it observes is projected to local `[e a v t m]` AST facts\n     9\t   (yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md §6.5) and committed as ONE atomic transaction\n    10\t   record through a `dao.space.transactor`, which allocates `t`; this\n    11\t   namespace supplies no clock.  Every row of a committed packet is\n    12\t   materialized into the `dao.jing` store in the same round, so its\n    13\t   `:yin/address` facts name content the store holds (yin.vm.linker.dht.md\n    14\t   5.1, rows every round).  After a round that committed, the covered\n    15\t   indexes are published through `transactor/publish!` into that round's\n    16\t   own fresh intake, the intake is drained into the `dao.jing` store, the\n    17\t   manifest is read back, and the intake is dropped: between rounds the\n    18\t   indexer retains its local transaction log and nothing of any\n    19\t   publication.\n    20\t\n    21\t   Cost, accepted as the price of the owner's every-round cadence\n    22\t   (2026-09-28): each publication rebuilds the covered indexes over the\n    23\t   whole retained history, and opening the round's transactor rescans\n    24\t   that history to derive `t`, so a round's index time grows linearly with\n    25\t   the session's committed code and a session's total grows\n    26\t   quadratically.  Memory does not: at most one publication is held, and\n    27\t   only during its round.  An incremental publish in `dao.space.index`\n    28\t   would remove the time growth; nothing here would need to change but\n    29\t   the call.\n    30\t\n    31\t   Every `e` is a transactor-local entity id; the only durable name in the\n    32\t   projection is the `:yin/address` fact each node occurrence carries back\n    33\t   to its row address.  `m` is a local metadata entity, one per program,\n    34\t   carrying `:db/op`, the shell's stable session token, the program's root\n    35\t   address, and the round.  Only code is indexed: no printed output, last\n    36\t   value, or evaluation result enters.\n    37\t\n    38\t   Loss is reported, never hidden, and never stops the evaluator (owner\n    39\t   ruling, 2026-09-28): a gap is counted on the observer (`:ingress-gaps`)\n    40\t   and marks the indexer `:lost?`, after which it consumes packets without\n    41\t   indexing any until reset rebuilds it; a packet that could not be\n    42\t   committed, or a publication that did not become readable, is recorded\n    43\t   under `:failure`, never counted as indexed.  `notice` renders what a\n    44\t   round lost for the shell's round result, and `status` is the\n    45\t   evaluator-independent view `repl-state` reports.  Everything here is a\n    46\t   session-composition value; reset and VM selection rebuild it with the\n    47\t   session.  Over a durable store a new process's indexer is seeded from\n    48\t   the recovered snapshot (`rehydrate`), and a rebuilt session's continues\n    49\t   the old one's index (`carry-over`), so `t` and entity allocation never\n    50\t   restart there.\"\n    51\t  (:require [dao.datom :as datom]\n    52\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    53\t            [dao.space.index :as index]\n    54\t            [dao.space.transactor :as transactor]\n    55\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    56\t            [dao.stream.memory-log :as memory-log]\n    57\t            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n    58\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    59\t            [yin.vm.macro :as macro]))\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t;; =============================================================================\n    63\t;; The §6.5 projection\n    64\t;; =============================================================================\n    65\t\n    66\t(defn- assign-local-ids\n    67\t  \"Give every node occurrence of `node`, the map AST rebuilt from row `id`,\n    68\t   a fresh local entity id as its `:eid`, pairing it with its row through\n    69\t   the §2.3 slot table.  Distinct occurrences of one shared row get distinct\n    70\t   ids, so `vm/ast->datoms` emits every occurrence exactly as it does for a\n    71\t   tree without `:eid`s.  `acc` is `[next-e addresses]`; answers\n    72\t   `[node' acc']`, `addresses` mapping each id to its row address.\"\n    73\t  [rows node id [next-e addresses]]\n    74\t  (let [row (get rows id)\n    75\t        slots (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar (:type node))\n    76\t        child (fn [acc child-node child-id]\n    77\t                (assign-local-ids rows child-node child-id acc))]\n    78\t    (reduce\n    79\t      (fn [[node acc] [i [field kind]]]\n    80\t        (let [slot (nth row (+ 2 i))]\n    81\t          (case kind\n    82\t            :node (let [[c acc'] (child acc (get node field) slot)]\n    83\t                    [(assoc node field c) acc'])\n    84\t            :nodes (let [[cs acc']\n    85\t                         (reduce (fn [[cs acc] [c cid]]\n    86\t                                   (let [[c' acc'] (child acc c cid)]\n    87\t                                     [(conj cs c') acc']))\n    88\t                                 [[] acc]\n    89\t                                 (map vector (get node field) slot))]\n    90\t                     [(assoc node field cs) acc'])\n    91\t            [node acc])))\n    92\t      [(assoc node :eid next-e) [(inc next-e) (assoc addresses next-e id)]]\n    93\t      (map-indexed vector slots))))\n    94\t\n    95\t\n    96\t(defn packet->tx-data\n    97\t  \"Project one expanded tree packet to transactor tx-data, allocating local\n    98\t   entity ids from `next-e`.  `provenance` is `{:session-token s :round r}`.\n    99\t\n   100\t   Answers `{:tx-data [...] :next-e n :meta-e m :root root}`: the metadata\n   101\t   entity's facts, then `vm/ast->datoms` of the expanded tree under `m`,\n   102\t   then one `[e :yin/address addr]` per node occurrence.  Every datom leaves\n   103\t   `t` nil, which the transactor stamps.\"\n   104\t  [packet next-e {:keys [session-token round]}]\n   105\t  (let [{:keys [root rows], :as row-set} (macro/packet->row-set packet)\n   106\t        meta-e next-e\n   107\t        [ast [next-e' addresses]] (assign-local-ids\n   108\t                                    rows\n   109\t                                    (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast row-set)\n   110\t                                    root\n   111\t                                    [(inc meta-e) {}])\n   112\t        facts (vm/ast->datoms ast {:m meta-e})\n   113\t        untimed (fn [e a v m] [e a v nil m])]\n   114\t    (when-let [stray (some (fn [[e]] (when (neg? e) e)) facts)]\n   115\t      (throw (ex-info \"projected node escaped local id assignment\"\n   116\t                      {:e stray, :root root})))\n   117\t    {:tx-data (-> [(untimed meta-e :db/op :db/assert datom/default-op)\n   118\t                   (untimed meta-e :yin.repl/session session-token\n   119\t                            datom/default-op)\n   120\t                   (untimed meta-e :yin.repl/root root datom/default-op)\n   121\t                   (untimed meta-e :yin.repl/round round datom/default-op)]\n   122\t                  (into (map (fn [[e a v _t m]] (untimed e a v m))) facts)\n   123\t                  (into (map (fn [[e addr]]\n   124\t                               (untimed e :yin/address addr meta-e)))\n   125\t                        (sort-by key addresses))),\n   126\t     :next-e next-e',\n   127\t     :meta-e meta-e,\n   128\t     :root root\n   129\t     :row-set row-set}))\n   130\t\n   131\t\n   132\t;; =============================================================================\n   133\t;; The indexer value\n   134\t;; =============================================================================\n   135\t\n   136\t(defn- memory-log\n   137\t  []\n   138\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n   139\t    (memory-log/create! {:dao.stream/type memory-log/transport-type})))\n   140\t\n   141\t\n   142\t(defn make-indexer\n   143\t  \"The indexer for one session: `observer`, attached to `program-out`\n   144\t   beside the evaluator's; `:local`, the complete-retention log its\n   145\t   transactions are committed to (dao.space.transactor requires memory-log\n   146\t   retention); and `content-store`, the `dao.jing` byte store publications\n   147\t   materialize into.  `session-token` is the shell's stable token, recorded\n   148\t   as provenance; `publish-opts` reach `transactor/publish!` as-is.\n   149\t\n   150\t   `after-publish` is `(fn [manifest-address])`, called after a round's\n   151\t   manifest is read back from the store and before the round is reported\n   152\t   published: the durable store's HEAD write, which is what makes the\n   153\t   round durably published (docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md).\n   154\t   Nil — the memory store — publishes exactly as before.\n   155\t\n   156\t   Between rounds that is all it holds.  A round that has code to commit\n   157\t   opens its `:publication` — a transactor over `:local` whose intake pool\n   158\t   is one fresh complete-retention intake — and drops it when the round\n   159\t   ends, so no earlier publication's payloads stay reachable from the\n   160\t   indexer (see `step`).\"\n   161\t  [{:keys [observer session-token content-store publish-opts after-publish]}]\n   162\t  {:observer observer\n   163\t   :local (memory-log)\n   164\t   :content-store content-store\n   165\t   :session-token session-token\n   166\t   :publish-opts publish-opts\n   167\t   :after-publish after-publish\n   168\t   :next-e datom/first-user-id\n   169\t   :transactions 0\n   170\t   :published 0\n   171\t   :published-payloads 0\n   172\t   :manifest-address nil\n   173\t   :lost? false\n   174\t   :failure nil})\n   175\t\n   176\t\n   177\t(defn- next-entity-id\n   178\t  \"One greater than the greatest entity or metadata-entity id `datoms`\n   179\t   use, never below `datom/first-user-id`.\"\n   180\t  [datoms]\n   181\t  (reduce (fn [next-e [e _a _v _t m]]\n   182\t            (cond-> next-e\n   183\t              (integer? e) (max (inc e))\n   184\t              (integer? m) (max (inc m))))\n   185\t          datom/first-user-id\n   186\t          datoms))\n   187\t\n   188\t\n   189\t(defn rehydrate\n   190\t  \"Seed a fresh indexer from a recovered durable snapshot, `{:manifest\n   191\t   address :datoms [...]}` (yin.repl.store's `:recovery`), before any\n   192\t   evaluation is admitted.  Its log becomes a fresh complete-retention\n   193\t   memory log holding the recovered datoms as transaction records, one\n   194\t   per original `t` in ascending order, each datom and its `t` preserved,\n   195\t   so the round's transactor keeps deriving the next `t` from it.  Entity\n   196\t   allocation resumes one past the greatest restored entity or metadata\n   197\t   id.  The manifest is the published one, covering every restored\n   198\t   transaction, so `q` answers from it before anything new is evaluated.\n   199\t   Restored facts keep their original session tokens and round metadata:\n   200\t   they are the datoms as committed.  A recovery without a manifest is an\n   201\t   empty index and leaves the indexer as it is.\"\n   202\t  [indexer {:keys [manifest datoms]}]\n   203\t  (if (nil? manifest)\n   204\t    indexer\n   205\t    (let [log (memory-log)\n   206\t          by-t (group-by index/datom-t datoms)\n   207\t          ts (sort (keys by-t))]\n   208\t      (doseq [t ts]\n   209\t        (let [answer (stream/append! log {:dao.space/transaction\n   210\t                                          {:t t, :datoms (vec (get by-t t))}})]\n   211\t          (when-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answer))\n   212\t            (throw (ex-info \"the recovered snapshot could not be rehydrated\"\n   213\t                            {:t t, :outcome answer})))))\n   214\t      (assoc indexer\n   215\t             :local log\n   216\t             :next-e (next-entity-id datoms)\n   217\t             :transactions (count ts)\n   218\t             :published (count ts)\n   219\t             :manifest-address manifest))))\n   220\t\n   221\t\n   222\t(defn carry-over\n   223\t  \"A rebuilt session's fresh `indexer`, continuing `previous`'s index: its\n   224\t   transaction log, entity allocation, counts, and published manifest.\n   225\t   `(reset)` and VM selection over a durable store use it, so a rebuild\n   226\t   never resets `t` or entity allocation and `q` keeps answering the\n   227\t   published index; the observer is the new session's, and a lost or\n   228\t   failed indexer is recovered by the rebuild as it is today.\"\n   229\t  [indexer previous]\n   230\t  (merge indexer\n   231\t         (select-keys previous [:local :next-e :transactions :published\n   232\t                                :published-payloads :manifest-address\n   233\t                                :unwritten])))\n   234\t\n   235\t\n   236\t(defn- open-publication\n   237\t  \"The round's transactor and the `dao.jing` pool observer over its intake.\n   238\t   `transactor/create!` derives the next `t` from `:local`'s retained\n   239\t   history, so transaction time continues across rounds.  The intake is\n   240\t   complete-retention: `publish-index!` appends every node blob before the\n   241\t   manifest and the round drains only after it returns, so an evicting\n   242\t   intake would lose the head of any publication larger than its capacity\n   243\t   and that publication could never complete.\"\n   244\t  [ix]\n   245\t  (if (:publication ix)\n   246\t    ix\n   247\t    (let [intake (memory-log)]\n   248\t      (assoc ix\n   249\t             :publication\n   250\t             {:transactor (transactor/create! {:local-stream (:local ix)\n   251\t                                               :intake-pool [intake]\n   252\t                                               :name \"yin.repl.index\"})\n   253\t              :pool (jing/observer-state\n   254\t                      [{:stream intake\n   255\t                        :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n   256\t                                  (stream/cursor intake\n   257\t                                                 :dao.stream/oldest))}])}))))\n   258\t\n   259\t\n   260\t(defn- write-rows\n   261\t  \"Put the rows of every committed program not yet written into the index\n   262\t   store, oldest first (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 5.1, owner decision 1: rows\n   263\t   every round), so `:yin/address` facts name content the store holds.\n   264\t   `:unwritten` holds those programs' row sets.  A put that fails stops\n   265\t   the writing: it and every later row set stay `:unwritten`, and the\n   266\t   round's failure is stage `:materialize`.  Once nothing is unwritten, a\n   267\t   `:materialize` failure is recovered and cleared.  No publication is\n   268\t   made while anything is unwritten, so a HEAD never moves over a missing\n   269\t   row.\"\n   270\t  [ix round]\n   271\t  (loop [ix ix]\n   272\t    (if-let [row-set (first (:unwritten ix))]\n   273\t      (let [failed (try (vm/materialize-tree! (:content-store ix) row-set)\n   274\t                        nil\n   275\t                        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   276\t                          {:round round\n   277\t                           :stage :materialize\n   278\t                           :root (:root row-set)\n   279\t                           :message (ex-message e)}))]\n   280\t        (if failed\n   281\t          (assoc ix :failure failed)\n   282\t          (recur (update ix :unwritten (comp vec rest)))))\n   283\t      (cond-> (dissoc ix :unwritten)\n   284\t        (= :materialize (:stage (:failure ix))) (dissoc :failure)))))\n   285\t\n   286\t\n   287\t(defn- commit\n   288\t  \"Commit one packet as one transaction; its rows join `:unwritten`, which\n   289\t   the round writes before it publishes (`write-rows`).  A packet that\n   290\t   could not be projected or committed is consumed and recorded as the\n   291\t   failure, never counted, and materializes nothing.\"\n   292\t  [ix packet round]\n   293\t  (try\n   294\t    (let [{:keys [tx-data next-e root row-set]}\n   295\t          (packet->tx-data packet\n   296\t                           (:next-e ix)\n   297\t                           {:session-token (:session-token ix), :round round})\n   298\t          answer (transactor/transact! (get-in ix [:publication :transactor])\n   299\t                                       tx-data)]\n   300\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answer))\n   301\t        [(-> ix\n   302\t             (assoc :next-e next-e)\n   303\t             (update :transactions inc)\n   304\t             (update :unwritten (fnil conj []) row-set))\n   305\t         true]\n   306\t        [(assoc ix\n   307\t                :failure {:round round\n   308\t                          :root root\n   309\t                          :stage :transact\n   310\t                          :outcome (:dao.stream/outcome answer)})\n   311\t         false]))\n   312\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   313\t      [(assoc ix\n   314\t              :failure {:round round\n   315\t                        :stage :project\n   316\t                        :message (ex-message e)})\n   317\t       false])))\n   318\t\n   319\t\n   320\t(defn- materialize\n   321\t  \"Drain the intake into the store until it blocks.  Answers how many\n   322\t   payloads it materialized and, when the drain met a gap or a defect, what\n   323\t   it met.  The pool is not kept: its intake is dropped with the round.\"\n   324\t  [content-store pool]\n   325\t  (loop [pool pool\n   326\t         n 0]\n   327\t    (let [{:keys [signal], :as r} (jing/observe-step! content-store pool)]\n   328\t      (case signal\n   329\t        :dao.stream/ok (recur (:state r) (inc n))\n   330\t        :dao.stream/blocked [n nil]\n   331\t        [n signal]))))\n   332\t\n   333\t\n   334\t(defn- publish\n   335\t  \"Publish the covered indexes over every committed transaction through\n   336\t   the round's transactor, drain its intake into the store, and read the\n   337\t   manifest back from it.  Only a publication whose manifest the store\n   338\t   answers becomes the reported one, covering `:published` transactions;\n   339\t   in durable mode the HEAD pointer moves — `after-publish` — only after\n   340\t   that read-back, so a HEAD never names a manifest the store cannot\n   341\t   answer, and a HEAD that cannot be written leaves the round reported\n   342\t   unpublished.\"\n   343\t  [ix round]\n   344\t  (try\n   345\t    (let [{:keys [transactor pool]} (:publication ix)\n   346\t          {:keys [manifest-address]} (transactor/publish! transactor\n   347\t                                                          (:publish-opts ix))\n   348\t          [n defect] (materialize (:content-store ix) pool)]\n   349\t      (if defect\n   350\t        (assoc ix :failure {:round round :stage :materialize :outcome defect})\n   351\t        (do (index/read-manifest (:content-store ix) manifest-address)\n   352\t            (when-some [write-head! (:after-publish ix)]\n   353\t              (write-head! manifest-address))\n   354\t            (assoc ix\n   355\t                   :manifest-address manifest-address\n   356\t                   :published (:transactions ix)\n   357\t                   :published-payloads n))))\n   358\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   359\t      (assoc ix\n   360\t             :failure {:round round :stage :publish :message (ex-message e)}))))\n   361\t\n   362\t\n   363\t(defn- consume\n   364\t  \"Advance the observer past every packet still on the medium, handing each\n   365\t   to `f` with the indexer; a gap marks the indexer lost, after which no\n   366\t   packet reaches `f`.\"\n   367\t  [indexer f]\n   368\t  (loop [ix indexer]\n   369\t    (let [{:keys [status batch] observer' :observer}\n   370\t          (observer/observe-next (:observer ix))\n   371\t          ix (assoc ix :observer observer')]\n   372\t      (case status\n   373\t        :ok (recur (if (:lost? ix) ix (f ix batch)))\n   374\t        :gap (recur (assoc ix :lost? true))\n   375\t        ix))))\n   376\t\n   377\t\n   378\t(defn step\n   379\t  \"The round's index step: observe every packet `program-out` still holds\n   380\t   for this observer, commit each through the round's publication, publish\n   381\t   when any was committed, then drop the publication — its transactor,\n   382\t   intake, and pool — so the indexer carries none of this round's payloads\n   383\t   into the next.  A gap is recovered across, counted on the observer's\n   384\t   `:ingress-gaps`, and marks the indexer lost: the missing packet and\n   385\t   every later one are never called indexed.\"\n   386\t  [indexer round]\n   387\t  (let [ix (consume indexer\n   388\t                    (fn [ix packet]\n   389\t                      (first (commit (open-publication ix) packet round))))\n   390\t        committed? (> (:transactions ix) (:transactions indexer))\n   391\t        ;; this round's rows and any an earlier round could not write,\n   392\t        ;; before any publication: no announcement names a missing row\n   393\t        ix (if committed? (write-rows ix round) ix)]\n   394\t    (dissoc (if (and committed? (empty? (:unwritten ix)))\n   395\t              (publish ix round)\n   396\t              ix)\n   397\t            :publication)))\n   398\t\n   399\t\n   400\t(defn commit-names\n   401\t  \"Commit the signed name envelopes `signed` -- each `{:envelope e :proof\n   402\t   p}` -- as ONE transaction, then publish the covered indexes at once,\n   403\t   the HEAD write included (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md 6.1): one\n   404\t   entity per envelope carrying `:yin.module/envelope` and\n   405\t   `:yin.module/proof`, with the session's metadata entity -- `:db/op`,\n   406\t   the session token and `round`, no program root -- in `m`.  A\n   407\t   transaction refused is recorded as the failure, like a packet's.\"\n   408\t  [indexer signed round]\n   409\t  (let [ix (open-publication indexer)\n   410\t        meta-e (:next-e ix)\n   411\t        untimed (fn [e a v m] [e a v nil m])\n   412\t        tx-data (into [(untimed meta-e :db/op :db/assert datom/default-op)\n   413\t                       (untimed meta-e :yin.repl/session (:session-token ix)\n   414\t                                datom/default-op)\n   415\t                       (untimed meta-e :yin.repl/round round datom/default-op)]\n   416\t                      (comp (map-indexed\n   417\t                              (fn [i {:keys [envelope proof]}]\n   418\t                                (let [e (+ meta-e 1 i)]\n   419\t                                  [(untimed e :yin.module/envelope envelope meta-e)\n   420\t                                   (untimed e :yin.module/proof proof meta-e)])))\n   421\t                            cat)\n   422\t                      signed)\n   423\t        answer (transactor/transact! (get-in ix [:publication :transactor])\n   424\t                                     tx-data)]\n   425\t    (dissoc (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome answer))\n   426\t              (let [ix (-> ix\n   427\t                           (assoc :next-e (+ meta-e 1 (count signed)))\n   428\t                           (update :transactions inc)\n   429\t                           (write-rows round))]\n   430\t                (cond-> ix (empty? (:unwritten ix)) (publish round)))\n   431\t              (assoc ix\n   432\t                     :failure {:round round\n   433\t                               :stage :transact\n   434\t                               :outcome (:dao.stream/outcome answer)}))\n   435\t            :publication)))\n   436\t\n   437\t\n   438\t(defn skip\n   439\t  \"Advance the observer past every packet still on the medium without\n   440\t   indexing it: a round that threw before its program ran executes nothing,\n   441\t   so nothing is indexed.  A gap still marks the indexer lost.\"\n   442\t  [indexer]\n   443\t  (consume indexer (fn [ix _packet] ix)))\n   444\t\n   445\t\n   446\t(defn status\n   447\t  \"The indexer's state as the shell reports it.  It depends on the programs\n   448\t   evaluated, never on which evaluator ran them or on the shell's token,\n   449\t   so every VM reports the same status for the same inputs.\"\n   450\t  [indexer]\n   451\t  {:transactions (:transactions indexer)\n   452\t   :published? (and (some? (:manifest-address indexer))\n   453\t                    (= (:published indexer) (:transactions indexer)))\n   454\t   :lost? (:lost? indexer)\n   455\t   :gaps (:ingress-gaps (:observer indexer) 0)\n   456\t   :failure (:failure indexer)})\n   457\t\n   458\t\n   459\t(defn notice\n   460\t  \"What the round from `before` to `after` must tell the user, or nil: a\n   461\t   lost indexer (the round's code was not indexed), or a new failure (the\n   462\t   round's code was not committed or its publication is not readable).\n   463\t   A failure's `:stage` is `:project`, `:transact`, `:materialize` or\n   464\t   `:publish`.\"\n   465\t  [before after]\n   466\t  (let [{:keys [stage outcome message]} (:failure after)]\n   467\t    (cond\n   468\t      (:lost? after)\n   469\t      (str \"Warning: the code index lost a program batch; this round's code\"\n   470\t           \" was not indexed, and indexing is suspended until (reset)\")\n   471\t\n   472\t      (and (= :materialize (:stage (:failure before))) (nil? (:failure after)))\n   473\t      (str \"Note: the code index caught up: rows of earlier rounds are now\"\n   474\t           \" written, and this round is published\")\n   475\t\n   476\t      (not= (:failure before) (:failure after))\n   477\t      (str \"Warning: this round's code is not in the published code index (\"\n   478\t           (name stage) \" failed\"\n   479\t           (when-let [detail (or message (some-> outcome name))]\n   480\t             (str \": \" detail))\n   481\t           \")\"))))\n     1\t(ns yin.vm.linker.sign\n     2\t  \"Ed25519 proofs for canonical module envelopes.\"\n     3\t  (:require [clojure.edn :as edn]\n     4\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n     5\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n     6\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n     7\t            #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:convert\" :as convert]\n     8\t                       [\"package:ed25519_edwards/ed25519_edwards.dart\" :as ed]])\n     9\t            #?@(:cljs [[goog.crypt :as crypt]]))\n    10\t  #?@(:cljd [(:import [\"dart:typed_data\" Uint8List])])\n    11\t  #?@(:cljd []\n    12\t      :clj [(:import [java.security KeyFactory KeyPairGenerator\n    13\t                      SecureRandom Signature]\n    14\t                     [java.security.spec NamedParameterSpec\n    15\t                      PKCS8EncodedKeySpec X509EncodedKeySpec])]))\n    16\t\n    17\t\n    18\t(def ^:private domain \"yin.module/envelope:v1\\n\")\n    19\t(def ^:private private-prefix \"302e020100300506032b657004220420\")\n    20\t(def ^:private public-prefix \"302a300506032b6570032100\")\n    21\t(def ^:private digits \"0123456789abcdef\")\n    22\t\n    23\t\n    24\t(defn- hex?\n    25\t  [n s]\n    26\t  (and (string? s)\n    27\t       (= n (count s))\n    28\t       (every? #(some? (str/index-of digits (str %))) s)))\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\t(defn- from-hex\n    32\t  [s]\n    33\t  (mapv (fn [[a b]]\n    34\t          (+ (* 16 (str/index-of digits (str a)))\n    35\t             (str/index-of digits (str b))))\n    36\t        (partition 2 s)))\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\t(defn- to-hex\n    40\t  [xs]\n    41\t  (apply str (mapcat (fn [x]\n    42\t                       (let [n (bit-and 255 x)]\n    43\t                         [(nth digits (quot n 16))\n    44\t                          (nth digits (mod n 16))]))\n    45\t                     xs)))\n    46\t\n    47\t\n    48\t(defn- host-bytes\n    49\t  [xs]\n    50\t  #?(:cljd (Uint8List.fromList (vec xs))\n    51\t     :clj (byte-array (map unchecked-byte xs))\n    52\t     :cljs (js/Uint8Array.from (clj->js xs))))\n    53\t\n    54\t\n    55\t(defn- utf8\n    56\t  [s]\n    57\t  #?(:cljd (convert/utf8.encode s)\n    58\t     :clj (.getBytes ^String s \"UTF-8\")\n    59\t     :cljs (crypt/stringToUtf8ByteArray s)))\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t(defn- message\n    63\t  [canonical]\n    64\t  (host-bytes (concat (utf8 domain) canonical)))\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\t#?(:cljd nil :clj\n    68\t   (defn- jvm-pair\n    69\t     [seed]\n    70\t     (let [bytes (host-bytes (from-hex seed))\n    71\t           random (proxy [SecureRandom] []\n    72\t                    (nextBytes\n    73\t                      [dst]\n    74\t                      (System/arraycopy bytes 0 dst 0 (alength dst))))\n    75\t           ;; SunEC's generator draws the 32 seed bytes from this random.\n    76\t           ;; The RFC vectors guard that provider-specific dependency.\n    77\t           generator (KeyPairGenerator/getInstance \"Ed25519\" \"SunEC\")]\n    78\t       (.initialize generator (NamedParameterSpec. \"Ed25519\") random)\n    79\t       (.generateKeyPair generator))))\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\t(defn public-of\n    83\t  [seed]\n    84\t  (when-not (hex? 64 seed)\n    85\t    (throw (ex-info \"Invalid Ed25519 seed\" {:reason :invalid-seed})))\n    86\t  #?(:cljd (to-hex (.-bytes (ed/public\n    87\t                              (ed/newKeyFromSeed\n    88\t                                (host-bytes (from-hex seed))))))\n    89\t     :clj (to-hex (take-last 32 (.getEncoded (.getPublic (jvm-pair seed)))))\n    90\t     :cljs (let [crypto (js/require \"crypto\")\n    91\t                 der (js/Buffer.from (str private-prefix seed) \"hex\")\n    92\t                 private (.createPrivateKey crypto #js {:key der :format \"der\"\n    93\t                                                        :type \"pkcs8\"})\n    94\t                 public (.createPublicKey crypto private)]\n    95\t             (to-hex (take-last 32 (.export public\n    96\t                                            #js {:format \"der\" :type \"spki\"}))))))\n    97\t\n    98\t\n    99\t(defn principal\n   100\t  [public]\n   101\t  (when-not (hex? 64 public)\n   102\t    (throw (ex-info \"Invalid Ed25519 public key\" {:reason :invalid-public})))\n   103\t  (str \"ed25519:\" public))\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t(defn generate\n   107\t  []\n   108\t  #?(:cljd (let [pair (ed/generateKey)]\n   109\t             {:seed (to-hex (take 32 (.-bytes (.-privateKey pair))))\n   110\t              :public (to-hex (.-bytes (.-publicKey pair)))})\n   111\t     :clj (let [seed (byte-array 32)]\n   112\t            (.nextBytes (SecureRandom.) seed)\n   113\t            (let [hex (to-hex seed)]\n   114\t              {:seed hex :public (public-of hex)}))\n   115\t     :cljs (let [seed (to-hex (.randomBytes (js/require \"crypto\") 32))]\n   116\t             {:seed seed :public (public-of seed)})))\n   117\t\n   118\t\n   119\t(defn- sign-bytes\n   120\t  [seed bytes]\n   121\t  #?(:cljd (ed/sign (ed/newKeyFromSeed (host-bytes (from-hex seed)))\n   122\t                    (host-bytes bytes))\n   123\t     :clj (let [factory (KeyFactory/getInstance \"Ed25519\" \"SunEC\")\n   124\t                encoded (host-bytes (from-hex (str private-prefix seed)))\n   125\t                private (.generatePrivate factory (PKCS8EncodedKeySpec. encoded))\n   126\t                signer (Signature/getInstance \"Ed25519\" \"SunEC\")]\n   127\t            (.initSign signer private)\n   128\t            (.update signer (host-bytes bytes))\n   129\t            (.sign signer))\n   130\t     :cljs (let [crypto (js/require \"crypto\")\n   131\t                 private (.createPrivateKey\n   132\t                           crypto #js {:key (js/Buffer.from\n   133\t                                              (str private-prefix seed) \"hex\")\n   134\t                                       :format \"der\" :type \"pkcs8\"})]\n   135\t             (.sign crypto nil (js/Buffer.from (host-bytes bytes)) private))))\n   136\t\n   137\t\n   138\t(defn sign-message\n   139\t  \"Sign raw bytes given as lowercase hex. Used for RFC 8032 conformance.\"\n   140\t  [seed message-hex]\n   141\t  (when-not (and (hex? 64 seed)\n   142\t                 (hex? (count message-hex) message-hex)\n   143\t                 (even? (count message-hex)))\n   144\t    (throw (ex-info \"Invalid Ed25519 vector\" {:reason :invalid-vector})))\n   145\t  (to-hex (sign-bytes seed (from-hex message-hex))))\n   146\t\n   147\t\n   148\t(defn sign-envelope\n   149\t  [seed envelope]\n   150\t  #?(:cljs (when-not (exists? js/require)\n   151\t             (throw (ex-info \"Ed25519 signing primitive unavailable\"\n   152\t                             {:reason :yin.link.sign/no-primitive}))))\n   153\t  (when-not (hex? 64 seed)\n   154\t    (throw (ex-info \"Invalid Ed25519 seed\" {:reason :invalid-seed})))\n   155\t  (when-not (= (principal (public-of seed))\n   156\t               (:yin.module/asserted-by envelope))\n   157\t    (throw (ex-info \"Envelope principal differs from key\"\n   158\t                    {:reason :principal-mismatch})))\n   159\t  {:yin.module/signature\n   160\t   (to-hex (sign-bytes seed (message (jing/canonical-bytes envelope))))})\n   161\t\n   162\t\n   163\t(defn verify-envelope\n   164\t  [public canonical signature]\n   165\t  (try\n   166\t    (if-not (and (hex? 64 public) (hex? 128 signature)\n   167\t                 (= (principal public)\n   168\t                    (:yin.module/asserted-by (cbor/decode canonical))))\n   169\t      false\n   170\t      (let [msg (message canonical)\n   171\t            sig (host-bytes (from-hex signature))]\n   172\t        #?(:cljd (ed/verify (ed/PublicKey. (host-bytes (from-hex public)))\n   173\t                            msg sig)\n   174\t           :clj (let [factory (KeyFactory/getInstance \"Ed25519\" \"SunEC\")\n   175\t                      encoded (host-bytes\n   176\t                                (from-hex (str public-prefix public)))\n   177\t                      pub (.generatePublic factory\n   178\t                                           (X509EncodedKeySpec. encoded))\n   179\t                      verifier (Signature/getInstance \"Ed25519\" \"SunEC\")]\n   180\t                  (.initVerify verifier pub)\n   181\t                  (.update verifier msg)\n   182\t                  (.verify verifier sig))\n   183\t           :cljs (let [crypto (js/require \"crypto\")\n   184\t                       pub (.createPublicKey\n   185\t                             crypto #js {:key (js/Buffer.from\n   186\t                                                (str public-prefix public)\n   187\t                                                \"hex\")\n   188\t                                         :format \"der\" :type \"spki\"})]\n   189\t                   (.verify crypto nil (js/Buffer.from msg) pub\n   190\t                            (js/Buffer.from sig))))))\n   191\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) _ false)))\n   192\t\n   193\t\n   194\t(defn key-text\n   195\t  [{:keys [seed public]}]\n   196\t  (pr-str {:version 1 :algorithm :ed25519\n   197\t           :seed seed :public public}))\n   198\t\n   199\t\n   200\t(defn key-from-text\n   201\t  [s]\n   202\t  (try\n   203\t    ;; The CLJD EDN reader rejects whitespace before a closing delimiter,\n   204\t    ;; so the wraps close directly after the trimmed text.  A trailing\n   205\t    ;; comment then swallows the closer and is refused on every host.\n   206\t    (let [s (str/trimr s)\n   207\t          forms (edn/read-string (str \"[\" s \"]\"))\n   208\t          key (when (= 1 (count forms)) (first forms))\n   209\t          wrapped (edn/read-string (str \"{:k \" s \"}\"))]\n   210\t      (cond\n   211\t        (or (not (map? key)) (not= wrapped {:k key}))\n   212\t        {:status :refused :reason :yin.link.sign/malformed-key}\n   213\t        (not= #{:version :algorithm :seed :public} (set (keys key)))\n   214\t        {:status :refused :reason :yin.link.sign/key-shape}\n   215\t        (not= 1 (:version key))\n   216\t        {:status :refused :reason :yin.link.sign/version}\n   217\t        (not= :ed25519 (:algorithm key))\n   218\t        {:status :refused :reason :yin.link.sign/algorithm}\n   219\t        (not (hex? 64 (:seed key)))\n   220\t        {:status :refused :reason :yin.link.sign/seed}\n   221\t        (not (hex? 64 (:public key)))\n   222\t        {:status :refused :reason :yin.link.sign/public}\n   223\t        (not= (:public key) (public-of (:seed key)))\n   224\t        {:status :refused :reason :yin.link.sign/public-mismatch}\n   225\t        :else {:seed (:seed key) :public (:public key)}))\n   226\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) _\n   227\t      {:status :refused :reason :yin.link.sign/malformed-key})))\n   123\t(defn- not-loaded\n   124\t  [node manifest-address]\n   125\t  (refused :yin.link.dht/not-loaded\n   126\t           {:address manifest-address\n   127\t            :load (dissoc (module-status node manifest-address) :value)}))\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(defn- loaded-closure\n   131\t  [node manifest-address]\n   132\t  (let [status (module-status node manifest-address)]\n   133\t    (when (and (= :loaded (:status status)) (= module-kind (:kind status)))\n   134\t      (:value status))))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t;; =============================================================================\n   138\t;; Names: the snapshot set and the fold (7.2, 7.3)\n   139\t;; =============================================================================\n   140\t\n   141\t(defn head\n   142\t  \"The manifest the HEAD of the node's directory names, or nil: a node\n   143\t   over a durable directory store (`dao.space.store`) has one once its\n   144\t   publisher has written it; any other node has none.\"\n   145\t  [node]\n   146\t  (when-some [dir (:durable-dir (dht/local node))]\n   147\t    (some-> (fs/read-file-text dir durable/head-name)\n   148\t            str/trim\n   149\t            edn/read-string\n   150\t            :manifest)))\n   151\t\n   152\t\n   153\t(defn snapshots\n   154\t  \"The node's snapshot set (7.2) as the sorted vector of its addresses:\n   155\t   the manifest its directory's HEAD names, when there is one, and every\n   156\t   index manifest whose load is `:loaded`.  Nothing else in the local\n   157\t   store is considered.\"\n   158\t  [node]\n   159\t  (vec (sort-by str (distinct (cond-> (vec (dht/loaded-indexes node))\n   160\t                                (head node) (conj (head node)))))))\n   161\t\n   162\t\n   163\t(defn- snapshot-datoms\n   164\t  \"The datoms of the snapshot `s`: a loaded index's, or HEAD's read from\n   165\t   the node's own store.\"\n   166\t  [node s]\n   167\t  (or (dht/loaded-datoms node s)\n   168\t      (index/read-datoms (dht/local node) s)))\n   169\t\n   170\t\n   171\t(defn- snapshot-events\n   172\t  \"The authority events of every snapshot, assembled per snapshot (an\n   173\t   entity id is local to its index) and concatenated in snapshot order,\n   174\t   each envelope with its proof once.\"\n   175\t  [node snapshot]\n   176\t  (into []\n   177\t        (comp (mapcat (fn [s]\n   178\t                        (authority/events-from-datoms\n   179\t                          (filter (fn [[_ a]]\n   180\t                                    (contains? #{:yin.module/envelope\n   181\t                                                 :yin.module/proof}\n   182\t                                               a))\n   183\t                                  (snapshot-datoms node s)))))\n   184\t              (distinct))\n   185\t        snapshot))\n   186\t\n   187\t\n   188\t(defn authority\n   189\t  \"The reader's authority from its composition (7.1): each declared\n   190\t   public key (64 lowercase hex) a principal whose proof is an Ed25519\n   191\t   signature (6.3), at `:seq-floor` 0, and `name-env`'s direct entries.\"\n   192\t  [{:keys [principals name-env]}]\n   193\t  {:principals (into {}\n   194\t                     (map (fn [public]\n   195\t                            [(sign/principal public)\n   196\t                             {:proof :yin.module/signature\n   197\t                              :key public\n   198\t                              :verify sign/verify-envelope\n   199\t                              :seq-floor 0}]))\n   200\t                     principals)\n   201\t   :name-env (or name-env {})})\n   202\t\n   203\t\n   204\t(defn- fold\n   267\t  [node authority n]\n   268\t  (let [folded (fold node authority)\n   269\t        entry (get-in folded [:env :names n])]\n   270\t    (cond\n   271\t      (= :ok (:status entry)) entry\n   272\t\n   273\t      (= :ambiguous-name (:reason entry))\n   274\t      (refused :ambiguous-name (merge {:name n}\n   275\t                                      (select-keys entry [:addresses :asserters])))\n   276\t\n   277\t      :else\n   278\t      (refused :absent {:name n :diagnostics (diagnostics-for folded n)}))))\n   279\t\n   280\t\n   281\t;; =============================================================================\n   282\t;; Dependency bindings (7.4)\n   283\t;; =============================================================================\n   284\t\n   285\t\n   286\t(defn dependency-bindings\n   287\t  \"One entry per requirement of the loaded closure of `manifest-address`,\n   288\t   in walk order: whether the dependency's name resolves, in the reader's\n   289\t   own name environment, to the address its publisher pinned.  `:binding`\n   290\t   is `:ok`, `:absent` (with the fold's `:diagnostics` for that name),\n   291\t   `:ambiguous` (`:addresses`, `:asserters`) or `:mismatch` (`:resolved`,\n   292\t   `:asserters`).  Refused `:yin.link.dht/not-loaded` unless the closure\n   293\t   is `:loaded`.\"\n   294\t  [node authority manifest-address]\n   295\t  (if-some [w (loaded-closure node manifest-address)]\n   296\t    (let [folded (fold node authority)]\n   297\t      (mapv (fn [{:keys [module name manifest]}]\n   298\t              (let [entry (get-in folded [:env :names name])\n   299\t                    base {:module module :name name :pinned manifest}\n   300\t                    asserters (get-in entry [:yin.link/provenance\n   301\t                                             :yin.module/asserted-by])]\n   302\t                (cond\n   303\t                  (= :ambiguous-name (:reason entry))\n   304\t                  (assoc base :binding :ambiguous\n   305\t                         :addresses (:addresses entry)\n   306\t                         :asserters (:asserters entry))\n   307\t\n   308\t                  (not= :ok (:status entry))\n   309\t                  (assoc base :binding :absent\n   310\t                         :diagnostics (diagnostics-for folded name))\n   311\t\n   312\t                  (= manifest (:address entry))\n   313\t                  (assoc base :binding :ok)\n   314\t\n   315\t                  :else\n   316\t                  (assoc base :binding :mismatch\n   317\t                         :resolved (:address entry)\n   318\t                         :asserters (or asserters [:composition])))))\n   319\t            (:requires w)))\n   320\t    (not-loaded node manifest-address)))\n   321\t\n   322\t\n   323\t;; =============================================================================\n   324\t;; Link (4.1 step 4)\n   325\t;; =============================================================================\n   326\t\n   327\t(defn link\n   328\t  \"`link-manifest` of `format-kw` through `manifest-address` over the\n   329\t   node's local store, `:verifying` with discharge deferred unless `opts`\n   330\t   says otherwise.  Refused `:yin.link.dht/not-loaded` unless the closure\n   331\t   is `:loaded`; a link refused `:absent` after it is a walker defect,\n   332\t   `:yin.link.dht/closure-incomplete`.\"\n   333\t  ([node manifest-address format-kw]\n   334\t   (link node manifest-address format-kw nil))\n   335\t  ([node manifest-address format-kw opts]\n   336\t   (let [format (some #(when (= format-kw (:format %)) %) publish/code-formats)]\n   337\t     (cond\n   338\t       (nil? (loaded-closure node manifest-address))\n   339\t       (not-loaded node manifest-address)\n   340\t\n   341\t       (nil? format)\n   342\t       (linker/refused :unsupported-format {:format format-kw})\n   343\t\n   344\t       :else\n   345\t       (let [res (publish/link-local (dht/local node) manifest-address format opts)]\n   346\t         (if (= :absent (:reason res))\n   347\t           (refused :yin.link.dht/closure-incomplete {:address (:address res)})\n   348\t           res))))))\n   270\t(defn- dht-link\n   271\t  \"Link the loaded closure of `address` over a local runtime on the\n   272\t   node's store (`yin.vm.linker/local-runtime`), `:verifying`, discharge\n   273\t   deferred.  A local store answers every content request at once, so no\n   274\t   attempt budget applies; an `:absent` refusal after the load is a\n   275\t   walker defect, `:yin.link.dht/closure-incomplete`.\"\n   276\t  [node request address]\n   277\t  (let [res (linker/link-manifest\n   278\t              (linker/local-runtime (dht/store node) {:formats formats})\n   279\t              address\n   280\t              (:yin.link/format request)\n   281\t              {}\n   282\t              {:contract (:yin.link/contract request)\n   283\t               :name (:yin.link/name request)\n   284\t               :derivation :verifying\n   285\t               :defer-discharge true})]\n   286\t    (cond\n   287\t      (linker/ok? res) {:status :ok\n   288\t                        :image {:value (:value res)}\n   289\t                        :manifest (:manifest res)\n   290\t                        :obligations (:obligations res)}\n   291\t      (= :absent (:reason res)) {:status :refused\n   292\t                                 :reason :yin.link.dht/closure-incomplete\n   293\t                                 :address (:address res)}\n   294\t      :else res)))\n   295\t\n   296\t\n   297\t(defn- dht-attempt\n   298\t  \"One attempt against the DHT source for the resolved `address`:\n   299\t   `{:node n :body b}`, `b` `::pending` with `:waits` the manifest whose\n   300\t   load the link waits on.  No record starts the load; `:loading` waits;\n   301\t   `:failed` is refused and forgotten, so a later require loads again;\n   302\t   `:loaded` checks the dependency bindings, the first that is not `:ok`\n   303\t   refusing before any link, then links.\"\n   304\t  [node authority request address]\n   305\t  (let [status (linker.dht/module-status node address)]\n   306\t    (cond\n   307\t      (nil? status) {:node (linker.dht/load-module node address)\n   308\t                     :body ::pending\n   309\t                     :waits address}\n   310\t\n   311\t      (= :loading (:status status)) {:node node, :body ::pending, :waits address}\n   312\t\n   313\t      (= :failed (:status status)) {:node (dht/forget node address)\n   314\t                                    :body (linker.dht/load-refusal status)}\n   315\t\n   316\t      :else\n   317\t      (let [bindings (linker.dht/dependency-bindings node authority address)\n   318\t            unbound (if (map? bindings)\n   319\t                      bindings\n   320\t                      (some (fn [b]\n   321\t                              (when-not (= :ok (:binding b))\n   322\t                                (merge {:status :refused\n   323\t                                        :reason :yin.link.dht/dependency-binding}\n   324\t                                       b)))\n   325\t                            bindings))]\n   326\t        {:node node\n   327\t         :body (or unbound (dht-link node request address))}))))\n   328\t\n   329\t\n   330\t(defn- answer\n   331\t  \"The response body for one link request under `:body`, or `::pending`\n   332\t   when nothing this round can answer it: no content source, an attempt\n   333\t   that spent its budget, or a DHT closure load not yet ended (its\n   334\t   manifest under `:waits`).  `:node` is the shell's DHT node after the\n   335\t   answer.  A request that is not by name is refused: the interpreter\n   336\t   serves what the shell's own VMs send, the by-name manifest requests\n   337\t   of section 7.2, and nothing else.\"\n   338\t  [source node request]\n   339\t  (let [name (:yin.link/name request)\n   340\t        dht? (= :dht (get-in source [:content :kind]))]\n   341\t    (cond\n   342\t      (nil? (:content source)) {:node node, :body ::pending}\n   343\t\n   344\t      (nil? name)\n   345\t      {:node node\n   346\t       :body {:status :refused, :reason :invalid-request,\n   347\t              :defect :yin.repl/name-required}}\n   348\t\n   349\t      dht?\n   350\t      (let [declared (authority source)\n   351\t            entry (linker.dht/resolve-name node declared name)]\n   352\t        (if (= :ok (:status entry))\n   353\t          (dht-attempt node declared request (:address entry))\n   354\t          {:node node, :body entry}))\n   355\t\n   356\t      :else\n   357\t      {:node node\n   358\t       :body (if-let [address (get (:name-env source) name)]\n   359\t               (attempt source request address)\n   360\t               {:status :refused, :reason :absent, :name name})})))\n   361\t\n   362\t\n   363\t(defn- respond!\n   364\t  \"Append `body` under the request's id on the response stream.  Returns\n   365\t   true when it landed, so the interpreter's cursor advances past the\n   366\t   request only then; a refused append leaves it to be re-read.\"\n   367\t  [pair request body]\n   368\t  (let [o (stream/append! (:responses pair)\n   369\t                          (assoc body :yin.link/id (:yin.link/id request)))]\n   370\t    (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome o))))\n   371\t\n   372\t\n   373\t(defn serve\n   374\t  \"One serve round of the interpreter over the link pair: read every\n   375\t   request `pair`'s cursor has not yet consumed and answer each in\n   376\t   request order, at most `budget` of them.  The first request nothing\n   377\t   can answer yet stops the round -- the requests behind it keep their\n   378\t   order -- and is reported under `:pending`; its cursor stays, so a\n   379\t   later round re-reads and re-attempts it.  A response the response\n   380\t   medium refuses reports its request pending the same way, and the\n   381\t   round reports no progress.  `dht` is the shell's DHT node, which a DHT\n   382\t   source reads and advances.  Returns\n   383\t   `{:pair pair :pending pending :progress? bool :dht node}`,\n   384\t   `:progress?` true when at least one response was appended, so the\n   385\t   shell knows the round moved something; a pending entry a DHT load\n   386\t   holds names that load's manifest under `:manifest`.\"\n   387\t  ([comp] (serve comp serve-budget))\n   388\t  ([{:keys [pair source dht]} budget]\n   389\t   (loop [pair pair\n   390\t          node dht\n293:(deftest separate-jvm-processes-exchange-content-over-loopback\n506:            (step \"(my.lib/f 1)\" #\"^(yin> )*4201$\" n)\n617:(defn- plain-clojure-leg\n667:              (is (= 4201 (vm/value answer)))))\n703:                       (ld/load-refusal (ld/module-status node nowhere))))))\n709:                    row (ld/load-refusal (ld/module-status node bad))]\n744:                       (ld/load-refusal (ld/module-status node elsewhere))))))))\n751:(deftest a-module-published-by-name-is-required-by-name-across-processes\n762:        (main/keygen! key-file)\n797:            (let [b (reader \"reader-b-jvm\" (jvm-command) (dirs 1) [public])\n799:                      (reader \"reader-b-node\" [\"node\" node-script] (dirs 2) [public]))\n829:                (plain-clojure-leg [x pa] manifest public)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
