{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba collab/1790837000000-engineer-linker-L5.claude-opus-5-5.report.md | tail -84; rg -n 'test-paths|test-dir|test-ns|ns-regexp' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-linker-l2/{deps.edn,shadow-cljs.edn,cljd.edn}; nl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-linker-l2/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '1280,1340p'; rg -n 'relevant|loaded|load-failed|checks|re-check' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-linker-l2/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | tail -30\"","aggregated_output":"   259\t  - `advance-load` no longer removes it, on the miss path or the found path.\n   260\t  - After every loading record has advanced in the step, `advance-loads` keeps only the causes of addresses some load is still fetching: `(update node :misses select-keys (fetching node))`. Every waiting load reads the cause, and none is retained once nothing waits.\n   261\t- **Test** (`test/dao/space/dht_test.cljc`, `loads-sharing-a-missing-blob-each-keep-its-cause`), three cases:\n   262\t  1. `/solo`: two loads ask for the same address in the same step. Both fail `{:failure :miss :address a :cause ::jing.dht/solo}`.\n   263\t  2. Completions spanning several steps: over a mesh with a silent peer, load 1 asks at reading 0, load 2 joins at reading 20, and load 3 at reading 40. All three fail with the same `::jing.dht/exhausted`, and `:misses` is empty afterwards. I first expected `/deadline`; with 10 ms steps the candidates run out first. I corrected my expectation; the shared cause, not `/gap`, is the property.\n   264\t  3. A load started after the first one failed asks again, and each keeps `/solo`.\n   265\t  - Before the fix: 4 failures, with the later loads reporting `/gap`.\n   266\t- **Mutations.**\n   267\t  - F2a, the destructive `dissoc` restored: 3 failures, the `/gap` regression.\n   268\t  - F2b, no prune after the step: 1 failure, the cause kept when nothing waits.\n   269\t\n   270\t### 3. An empty export list is the canonical no-op module, as data (`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`)\n   271\t\n   272\t- **Fix.**\n   273\t  - New public `yin.vm.linker.publish/no-op-tree`, which is `{:type :literal :value nil}`: one `nil` literal that defines nothing.\n   274\t  - `sequenced` answers it for zero programs instead of popping an empty vector.\n   275\t  - So `module-from-index` with `:exports []` answers `{:name n :ast no-op-tree :exports #{} :requires {} :primitives {}}`, whatever the index holds. It publishes, and links ok on all four formats.\n   276\t  - §5.3's \"One tree\" bullet states the rule.\n   277\t- **Plain test** (`test/yin/vm/linker/publish_test.cljc`, `an-empty-export-list-is-the-canonical-no-op-module`, all three hosts):\n   278\t  - the exact spec;\n   279\t  - the same spec from a different index;\n   280\t  - `publish-module!` gives a segment address with all four `:links` `:ok` and `:yin.module/exports #{}`.\n   281\t  - Before the fix: `IllegalStateException: Can't pop empty vector`.\n   282\t- **REPL test** (`dht_end_to_end_test.cljc`, `an-empty-export-list-publishes-the-no-op-module-at-the-prompt`): `(yin.link/publish (quote empty.lib) (quote []))` answers `{:module empty.lib … :links {all four :ok}}` as data. A reader hydrating the publisher's HEAD then requires `empty.lib` by name on all four VMs.\n   283\t- **Mutation F3,** the empty branch removed: the plain test errors with `Can't pop empty vector`, and the REPL test fails 6 assertions. The REPL printed `Error: Can't pop empty vector`, and the reader's require was `:absent` on every VM.\n   284\t\n   285\tEvery mutation was reverted. `git status` shows only intended changes. Files this round: `src/cljc/{dao/space/dht,yin/vm/linker/dht,yin/vm/linker/publish}.cljc`, `test/{dao/space/dht_test,yin/vm/linker/dht_test,yin/vm/linker/publish_test,yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test}.cljc`, and `docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md` (§5.3, §7.3).\n   286\t\n   287\t### Lanes (final code, all foreground, all to their verdict)\n   288\t\n   289\t| Lane | Verdict |\n   290\t|---|---|\n   291\t| kondo on all 9 changed `.clj`/`.cljc` files | errors 0, warnings 0 |\n   292\t| `bb test:cljs` | **Ran 2609 tests, 90374 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors** (`dao.space.dht-test`, `yin.vm.linker.dht-test`, `…dht-end-to-end-test`, `…publish-test` all ran) |\n   293\t| `bb build:yin-repl-peer` | built |\n   294\t| `bb test:cljd` (after `rm -rf test/cljd-out`) | **+2564: All tests passed!** (+4: the four new tests) |\n   295\t| `bb build:yin-repl-node` | built |\n   296\t| JVM `clojure -M:test` in three regex chunks | 1348/211266, 1226/12111, 122/938: **2696 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**. The chunks cover all 168 namespaces, including `yin.repl.dht-process-test`. |\n   297\t\n   298\t## Fix round 4 (gpt-6.1-sol r3: L5 GRANTED; epic withheld on one MEDIUM, `1790846000000-architect-linker-epic-review-r3.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md`)\n   299\t\n   300\t### The defect\n   301\t\n   302\t`yin.vm.linker/manifest-defect` is the schema-1 validator that the closure walker calls (`closure.cljc` `walk-module`). It called `(vals (:yin.module/index manifest))` without checking the shape first. So a correctly hashed manifest whose optional index was `42`, `[1]` or `\"bad\"` threw inside the validator. Three things followed:\n   303\t- the walk was not total;\n   304\t- the staged load reported `:dao.space.dht/walk-threw` with `:address nil`, instead of `:manifest-defect` naming the manifest;\n   305\t- `publish-module!` with such a manifest under `:requires` threw instead of refusing as data.\n   306\t\n   307\t### Fix (`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc`, 5 lines)\n   308\t\n   309\tThe index stays optional. When present and not nil, it must be a map; otherwise the validator answers `{:rule :manifest-shape :key :yin.module/index}`. Only after that check does it look at the values, as before. Neither `closure.cljc` nor `publish.cljc` needed a change: both already turn the validator's defect into data. The walker gives `:invalid :manifest-defect`, and publication gives `/invalid-requirement`.\n   310\t\n   311\t### Scan for other assumption-throws on optional or any manifest fields\n   312\t\n   313\tI made the scan executable instead of reading the code by eye. `the-manifest-validator-is-total-over-every-key` (in `closure_test`) checks every manifest key plus the optional index. Each key gets 8 malformed values: `42 [1] \"bad\" #{1} '(1) :k {1 2} [[1 2]]`, which is 88 cases. For each, the validator must answer a defect map and not throw. The manifest is then materialized and walked, and the walk must answer `:invalid` with `:manifest-defect` naming that address.\n   314\t- **Result before the fix:** only `:yin.module/index` threw, for 7 of its 8 values (`{1 2}` already gave a defect). Every other key already answered a defect for every value: each map-valued key is checked with `map?`/`set?`/`symbol?` before it is used, and the reserved-name scan runs only after the declaration keys pass.\n   315\t- **Result after the fix:** all 88 cases are a defect, and every walk is total.\n   316\t\n   317\t### Regressions (tests first; all cross-host .cljc)\n   318\t\n   319\t| Test | Asserts | Before the fix |\n   320\t|---|---|---|\n   321\t| `closure_test/a-malformed-optional-index-is-a-manifest-defect-naming-the-manifest` (42, [1], \"bad\") | validator → `{:rule :manifest-shape :key :yin.module/index}`; **direct walk** → `{:outcome :invalid :address m :role :manifest :path [m] :defect {:code :manifest-defect :detail {...}}}` | 3 failures + 3 errors (`ClassCastException`, `Don't know how to create ISeq`) |\n   322\t| `closure_test/the-manifest-validator-is-total-over-every-key` | the scan above | 7 + 7 failures, all `:yin.module/index` |\n   323\t| `linker/dht_test/a-malformed-optional-index-fails-the-load-as-a-manifest-defect` | **staged load** → `load-refusal` = `{:status :refused :reason :descriptor-defect :address m :code :manifest-defect :detail {:rule :manifest-shape :key :yin.module/index}}`, exactly one `:load-failed` | 3 failures (was `walk-threw`, `:address nil`) |\n   324\t| `publish_test/a-required-manifest-with-a-malformed-index-refuses-as-data` | **publication** requiring it → `{:status :refused :reason :yin.link.publish/invalid-requirement :name dep}`, nothing written | 3 failures (threw) |\n   325\t\n   326\t### Mutations\n   327\t\n   328\t- **Original code restored** (the map check removed): every regression above fails, 17 failures + 3 errors in `closure_test` alone. This includes the 7 walk-totality assertions.\n   329\t- **Mutation G**, a non-map index silently accepted (no throw, no defect): 16 failures across the direct walk, the staged load and the scan. The publication test still passes under G, and that is correct: the requirement walk refuses `/invalid-requirement` later, at the missing index entry. The original throwing code does fail it, 3 failures in the red run.\n   330\t\n   331\tReverted. `git diff src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc` is the 5-line fix only.\n   332\t\n   333\t### Lanes (final code, all foreground, all to their verdict)\n   334\t\n   335\t| Lane | Verdict |\n   336\t|---|---|\n   337\t| kondo on all 11 changed `.clj`/`.cljc` files of the branch | errors 0, warnings 0 |\n   338\t| `bb test:cljs` | **Ran 2613 tests, 90633 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors** (`closure-test`, `dht-test` and `publish-test` ran) |\n   339\t| `bb build:yin-repl-peer` | built |\n   340\t| `bb test:cljd` (after `rm -rf test/cljd-out`) | **+2568: All tests passed!** (+4: the four new tests) |\n   341\t| `bb build:yin-repl-node` | built |\n   342\t| JVM `clojure -M:test` in three regex chunks | 1348/211266, 1230/12370, 122/938: **2700 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**. The chunks cover all 168 namespaces, including `yin.repl.dht-process-test`. |\nrg: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-linker-l2/cljd.edn: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n  1280\t                             (:reason %))\n  1281\t                 (:wait-set vm))))\n  1282\t\n  1283\t\n  1284\t(defn- carry-link-identity\n  1285\t  \"The round's base VM with the link identity `used` has already minted\n  1286\t   carried forward: link ids `[origin counter]` and install-child origin\n  1287\t   tags are minted once and never reused on a pair (yin.vm.linker.md\n  1288\t   section 7.2), and the shell's rollback to the round's base -- whose\n  1289\t   counters never advanced -- must not let a later require or install\n  1290\t   mint an identity the pair has already answered.\"\n  1291\t  [base used]\n  1292\t  (let [n (max (or (:id-counter base) 0) (or (:id-counter used) 0))\n  1293\t        o (max (or (:origins base) 0) (or (:origins used) 0))]\n  1294\t    (cond-> base\n  1295\t      (pos? n) (assoc :id-counter n)\n  1296\t      (pos? o) (assoc :origins o))))\n  1297\t\n  1298\t\n  1299\t(defn- link-raise\n  1300\t  \"The raise of a resumed link wait, carrying the identity the parked\n  1301\t   evaluation has minted so far -- the counters of the VM the raise\n  1302\t   interrupted, whose every earlier run is in them -- so a rollback\n  1303\t   cannot reuse it.  It carries the query interpreter's pair too: the\n  1304\t   requests it has answered stay answered when the shell rolls back.\"\n  1305\t  [error vm state]\n  1306\t  (ex-info (or (ex-message error) \"Link failed\")\n  1307\t           (assoc (or (ex-data error) {})\n  1308\t                  ::link-counter (:id-counter vm)\n  1309\t                  ::link-origins (:origins vm)\n  1310\t                  ::query-pair (:query-pair state)\n  1311\t                  ::link-pair (:link-pair state)\n  1312\t                  ::dht (:dht state)\n  1313\t                  ::indexer (:indexer state))))\n  1314\t\n  1315\t\n  1316\t(defn- carry-served\n  1317\t  \"`state` rolled back by a link raise, keeping what the interpreters\n  1318\t   already concluded: the query pair, the link pair past every request\n  1319\t   answered, the DHT node a load started or forgot on, and the indexer\n  1320\t   a `yin.link/publish` committed its name envelopes through.\"\n  1321\t  [state d]\n  1322\t  (cond-> state\n  1323\t    (::query-pair d) (assoc :query-pair (::query-pair d))\n  1324\t    (::link-pair d) (assoc :link-pair (::link-pair d))\n  1325\t    (contains? d ::dht) (assoc :dht (::dht d))\n  1326\t    (::indexer d) (assoc :indexer (::indexer d))))\n  1327\t\n  1328\t\n  1329\t(defn- link-context\n  1330\t  \"What a `yin.link` call is answered under (yin.repl.query/serve): the\n  1331\t   reader's authority, the publisher's key, and the requesting VM's\n  1332\t   primitives and module registry -- the modules it linked are derived\n  1333\t   from it, never recorded -- and the round.\"\n  1334\t  [state vm]\n  1335\t  {:authority (link/authority (:link-source state))\n  1336\t   :key (:dht-key state)\n  1337\t   :primitives (:primitives vm)\n  1338\t   :modules (:modules vm)\n  1339\t   :round (:round state)})\n  1340\t\n122:   or one re-check of a pending run.  A query is answered in the round\n656:  \"The run step the evaluator observer hands each loaded program: run the\n811:   require parks and after each re-check that leaves the run pending,\n848:   `:dht-key` is the publisher's stable key `{:seed :public}`, loaded\n1350:   completed an install -- the fact the pending run's `:checks` resets\n1504:   when the require parks, and after each re-check that leaves it so;\n1505:   never on a re-check that completes it (yin.repl.link-policy.md\n1525:                              :checks (or (:checks parked) 0)\n1565:   line re-checks the link, the host may step one itself with\n1576:                           :checks 0})\n1811:   re-check.\"\n1851:  \"One bounded re-check of the shell's `:pending-run`: serve the\n1855:   the link policy when the re-check leaves the run pending, `:checks`\n1856:   counting this pending run's re-checks that made no progress and\n1857:   resetting on one that did, or, when the re-check raised the link's\n1873:          (let [checks (if progress? 0 (inc (or (:checks parked) 0)))\n1877:                                       :checks checks)\n1904:  \"One re-check of the shell's `:pending-run` without an input line --\n1908:   pending.  A re-check that completes the run folds the retained lines\n1919:  \"The host ticker's re-check of a pending run over a DHT link source\n1921:   `events` -- one tick's `dao.space.dht/step` events -- hold a `:loaded`\n1922:   or `:load-failed` event for a manifest a pending link waits on.  Any\n1924:   answers `[state nil]` with `state` itself: no re-check, no `:checks`.\"\n1928:                (and (contains? #{:loaded :load-failed} (:dao.space.dht/event e))\n1936:  \"One bounded re-check of the shell's `:pending-run` behind a typed\n1954:    ;; A require is still pending: re-check it first.  While it stays\n1994:   name (`:manual` or `:fn`) and the pending run's `:checks`, so a host\n2024:                         :checks (or (:checks parked) 0)})\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
